WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

8
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:24.550
Hello.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.890
Happy finale part two.
大结局第二部分快乐。

10
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.910
This is really it.
这真的是最后了。

11
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:36.430
This is season nine, episode 27, written by Greg Daniels, directed by Ken Kwapis.
这是第九季第27集，由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧，肯·卡皮斯执导。

12
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.650
Would you like a summary?
你想听听剧情梗概吗？

13
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:39.750
I would.
我想听。

14
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.070
All right.
好的。

15
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.250
Dwight and Angela are getting married.
德怀特和安吉拉要结婚了。

16
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.690
Kelly and Ryan are going to reunite.
凯莉和瑞安要重归于好了。

17
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.150
Nellie gets the baby she's been hoping for.
奈莉终于得到了她梦寐以求的孩子。

18
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.630
Pam and Jim make a very big decision about their future.
帕姆和吉姆对他们的未来做出了一个重大决定。

19
00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:00.750
And everyone at Dunder Mifflin gathers for one last night together.
邓德·米福林的所有员工聚在一起，度过了最后一个夜晚。

20
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.970
And this, you guys, remember when Greg asked us all what we hoped for our characters?
还有这个，大家还记得格雷格问我们每个人对自己的角色有什么期待吗？

21
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.450
Mine was, I hoped that Angela and Dwight would end up together.
我的期待是，希望安吉拉和德怀特能终成眷属。

22
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.370
So I love watching this.
所以我很喜欢看这一集。

23
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.270
It's so awesome.
太棒了。

24
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.710
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

25
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.130
Well, fast fact number one, Angela, is your look back moment.
好了，第一个速览事实，安吉拉，是你的回顾时刻。

26
00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:20.750
All right.
好的。

27
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.190
This is our final look back.
这是我们最后一次回顾了。

28
00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.610
You know, this is the bonus feature on disc four for season nine.
你知道，这是第九季第四张光盘上的花絮内容。

29
00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.890
And when I was watching all of it,
当我看完所有内容时，

30
00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:38.130
one of the things that really stood out to me was when everyone reflected on what the writers meant to the show and what Greg Daniels meant to everyone.
有一件事让我印象深刻，那就是每个人都在反思编剧对这部剧的意义，以及格雷格·丹尼尔斯对每个人的意义。

31
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.350
Let's listen.
让我们来听听。

32
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.190
First and foremost, it's a writer's show.
首先，这是一部编剧主导的剧集。

33
00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.350
And we really owe everything to the writers on this.
我们真的要把一切归功于这部剧的编剧们。

34
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.570
We also owe the writers, and especially Greg Daniels,
我们也欠编剧们，尤其是格雷格·丹尼尔斯，

35
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:59.730
a big debt of gratitude in that they trust the actors enough to let us play with their lines and improvise off of them and come up with other line ideas and pitches.
一份深深的感激，因为他们足够信任演员，让我们能够发挥台词并进行即兴创作，提出其他的台词想法和建议。

36
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.130
You don't get to do that on a lot of other TV shows.
在很多其他电视剧里你可没机会这么做。

37
00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.850
I think what helped it push through was a phenomenal cast and really great writing staff.
我认为推动它成功的因素是出色的演员阵容和非常优秀的编剧团队。

38
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.950
The perfect man for the job in Greg Daniels.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯是这份工作的完美人选。

39
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:17.450
Greg Daniels said in our first meeting, he's like, you know, American comedy is like this big ship, you know, a big, like, cruise liner.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯在我们的第一次会议上说，他说，你知道，美式喜剧就像一艘大船，你知道，就像一艘大型邮轮。

40
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:23.150
And if you can just point it one degree in the right direction, you can make a big, big difference.
如果你能让它向正确的方向转动一度，就能产生非常、非常大的影响。

41
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.510
You can't turn comedy that sharply.
你不能让喜剧转弯转得太急。

42
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:34.030
And I feel like that's what The Office did, is it took American comedy and it turned it one degree in the right direction.
我觉得《办公室》所做的就是这样，它带着美式喜剧向正确的方向转动了一度。

43
00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.910
At the time, comedy was very silly.
当时，喜剧非常无厘头。

44
00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.670
And there were a lot of very broad shows on the air.
电视上有很多非常夸张的节目。

45
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:44.750
And I think it was just the perfect time for reality to hit comedy.
我认为当时正是现实主义进入喜剧界的绝佳时机。

46
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:50.010
I think that there was something sort of like it was lightning in a bottle for the entire cast and the entire creative team.
我觉得这就像是整个演员阵容和整个创意团队的一次灵光一现。

47
00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:55.070
It's kind of a troupe of people who understand writing and performing all at the same time.
这群人既懂创作又懂表演，他们就像一个剧团。

48
00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.250
I spent more time here than I did on the set.
我在这里待的时间比在片场的时间还多。

49
00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.310
I spent more time here than I did at home.
我在这里待的时间比在家里还多。

50
00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.530
I definitely spent more hours here over the past 10 years than anywhere else in the world.
在过去的十年里，我在这里度过的时间绝对比世界上任何其他地方都多。

51
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.310
And it's not a very pretty place to be.
而且那地方环境并不怎么好。

52
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.390
But there was a lot of laughter and a lot of great ideas.
但那里充满了欢声笑语和许多绝妙的点子。

53
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.850
Well, Greg really was the visionary behind this show.
格雷格确实是这部剧背后的远见者。

54
00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:30.910
It was not an easy thing to adapt something that was only 13 episodes long, but a brilliant concept, and turn it into this 201 episodes of American television.
要把一部只有13集但概念极其出色的剧集改编成201集的美国电视剧，这绝非易事，但他做到了。

55
00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.330
I mean, that was Greg.
我是说，这就是格雷格。

56
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.010
Yeah.
没错。

57
00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.610
And also our writers.
还有我们的编剧们。

58
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.210
He assembled such an amazing team.
他组建了一支如此出色的团队。

59
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:45.750
And, you know, as Jen and I have done this rewatch, those of you that listen know how gracious the writing staff has been and Greg.
而且，你知道，正如珍和我在做重温节目时所说，听过节目的朋友们都知道编剧团队和格雷格有多么慷慨。

60
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.070
They've come on this show.
他们来到我们的节目中。

61
00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.490
They have sent us in answers and audio clips.
他们给我们发来了答案和音频片段。

62
00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.210
And we're just so appreciative to them.
我们对此深表感激。

63
00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.490
Well, Lady, you shared in our book that you had a writing professor who said,
对了，女士，你在书中分享过，你有一位写作教授曾说过，

64
00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.290
If something is a pleasure to do, it's a pleasure to watch.
如果一件事做起来是一种享受，那么看的人也会觉得是一种享受。

65
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.390
And I think that's what BJ was saying in that clip.
我想这正是BJ在那个片段里想表达的意思。

66
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:09.290
Like, it was my pleasure to sit in this dumpy writer's room for 10 years.
就像是，能在那个破旧的编剧室里坐上10年，对我来说是一种享受。

67
00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.950
If you watch it on the DVD, he is in the writer's room.
如果你看DVD的话，他就在编剧室里。

68
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.910
And there's not much there, you know.
那里其实没什么东西，你知道的。

69
00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:15.370
No, no.
不，没有。

70
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.050
But it is true.
但这是真的。

71
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.630
We just all had such a joyful time doing this show.
我们大家在制作这部剧时都度过了一段非常快乐的时光。

72
00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.530
And I think people feel it when they watch it.
我想观众在观看时也能感受到这一点。

73
00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:26.070
Yeah.
是的。

74
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.790
Well, Angela, I loved your lookbacks.
安吉拉，我很喜欢你的回顾视频。

75
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:29.590
Thanks.
谢谢。

76
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.970
I enjoyed watching that.
我看得津津有味。

77
00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.530
I couldn't watch it, everybody.
大家，我没法看那个视频。

78
00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.070
I told Angela, I'm like, I'll be a puddle.
我告诉安吉拉，我说，我会哭成泪人的。

79
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.430
I can't do it.
我做不到。

80
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.350
I said, Jenna, do you want to watch it together?
我说，珍娜，你要一起看吗？

81
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.810
And you were just like, no.
而你当时就说，不。

82
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.510
Well, I was a puddle.
好吧，我确实哭成了泪人。

83
00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.230
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

84
00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:50.050
I'll say I haven't watched the finale until we had to watch it to break it down.
我得说，在为了拆解剧情而不得不看之前，我一直没看过大结局。

85
00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.390
Because I don't know if this is true.
因为我不知道这是否属实。

86
00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.830
And I actually wish we would have asked Billie Eilish this.
我真希望我们当时问过比莉·艾利什这个问题。

87
00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.590
I know some people who will watch the whole series, but they won't watch the finale.
我知道有些人会看完整个系列，但就是不看大结局。

88
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.610
Oh, man.
天哪。

89
00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.910
They're missing some really good nuggets.
他们错过了一些非常精彩的片段。

90
00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:05.750
I know.
我知道。

91
00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:06.230
I know.
我知道。

92
00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.870
And actually, I'm glad now that I've seen it.
说实话，我现在很高兴我看了。

93
00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:09.410
But yeah.
但确实。

94
00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.730
Well, I'll tell you what I did after I watched The Look Back.
我告诉你我在看完回顾视频后做了什么。

95
00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.450
And I recommend that you do this because it's really emotional.
我建议你们也这样做，因为这真的很感人。

96
00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:19.510
I then watched the season nine bloopers.
我接着看了第九季的NG花絮。

97
00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:20.830
Oh, no.
噢，不。

98
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.730
And then I was just laughing.
然后我就一直在笑。

99
00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.230
So, I went from tearing up to laughter.
所以我从热泪盈眶转变成了开怀大笑。

100
00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.290
And that's the way you got to do it.
这才是你应该有的观看方式。

101
00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:28.290
All right.
好的。

102
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.630
Well, let's move on to fast fact number two.
那么，让我们进入第二个速览事实。

103
00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.430
I'm calling this one Wedding Weather.
我把它称为“婚礼天气”。

104
00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:34.030
Yeah.
没错。

105
00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:38.430
We shot all of Angela and Dwight's wedding at Big Sky Ranch.
安吉拉和德怀特的婚礼全是在大天空牧场拍摄的。

106
00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.370
We shot for three days at the ranch.
我们在牧场拍摄了三天。

107
00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.150
We shot on a Thursday, a Friday, and a Sunday.
拍摄时间分别是周四、周五和周日。

108
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.410
Thursday was actually my birthday.
周四那天其实是我的生日。

109
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.490
Oh, yeah.
哦，是吗。

110
00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.150
That's right.
没错。

111
00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.070
It was also the day Steve was there.
那天也是史蒂夫在场的一天。

112
00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:51.170
Oh.
哦。

113
00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.650
So, that was a really, really fun memory for me from that birthday.
所以，那是我那个生日里一段非常、非常美好的回忆。

114
00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.390
But there was an issue.
但当时出了个问题。

115
00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.930
Like any real wedding, we couldn't control the weather.
就像任何真实的婚礼一样，我们无法控制天气。

116
00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.130
And it was crazy windy.
风大得离谱。

117
00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.090
It was cold.
天气很冷。

118
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.390
It rained.
还下雨了。

119
00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.870
The high was 61.
最高气温只有61华氏度。

120
00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.270
The low was 45.
最低气温是45华氏度。

121
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:11.210
Yeah.
是啊。

122
00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.690
I remember them being worried the tent would blow away.
我记得他们当时很担心帐篷会被吹走。

123
00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.250
They were waiting it down.
他们一直在加固帐篷。

124
00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.970
The lanterns were swaying.
灯笼都在摇晃。

125
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.270
You saw the cloud bank rolling in.
你能看到云层滚滚而来。

126
00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.950
Well, I remember wondering, are we able to shoot this?
嗯，我记得当时在想，我们还能拍吗？

127
00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:26.330
Yeah.
是啊。

128
00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:31.250
Because the sky was very, very gloomy and ominous.
因为天空看起来非常、非常阴沉且不祥。

129
00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:39.230
And Matt Soane actually had to put up all these giant lights and like floodlights in order to try to brighten up everything.
马特·索恩不得不架起所有这些巨大的灯光和泛光灯，试图把一切照亮。

130
00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.070
It was dark.
天很黑。

131
00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:40.950
It was.
确实。

132
00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:41.450
Yeah.
是啊。

133
00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:47.330
But the call sheets for these three days, they said, we will shoot rain or shine.
但这三天的通告单上写着：无论风雨，照常拍摄。

134
00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.450
Please be prepared.
请做好准备。

135
00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.370
Yep.
没错。

136
00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:54.830
And we have some great, great pictures that really showcase the windy conditions.
我们有一些很棒的照片，真实展现了当时大风的天气状况。

137
00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.010
I mean, I have one of the clouds rolling in.
我是说，我有一张云层滚滚而来的照片。

138
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:03.650
I don't know if you remember, Jenna, but my veil kept blowing all over my face.
珍娜，我不记得你是否还记得，但我的头纱一直被吹到脸上。

139
00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:03.990
I do.
我记得。

140
00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.910
I have a picture of me and John and the veil is about to wrap around us.
我有一张我和约翰的照片，头纱快要把我们缠住了。

141
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:14.190
But our favorite, hands down, is a photo we discovered when we wrote our book, The Office BFFs.
但我们最喜欢的，毫无疑问，是我们写书《办公室闺蜜》时发现的一张照片。

142
00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:21.490
I took the picture standing in Angela Martin's shallow grave of everyone looking back at me.
我当时站在安吉拉·马丁的浅坟里，拍下了大家回头看我的样子。

143
00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:25.610
I really wanted to remember what I saw on Angela's wedding day.
我真的很想记住我在安吉拉婚礼那天看到的景象。

144
00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.590
And I took that picture and I never thought anything about it.
我拍了那张照片，当时也没多想。

145
00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.370
You know, we looked at it.
你知道，我们看过它。

146
00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.390
I put it in a scrapbook.
我把它放进了剪贴簿里。

147
00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:37.050
But when we started to do our book, we were really zooming in on pictures to make sure the image was good, the quality was good.
但当我们开始写书时，我们真的会放大照片来确保图像清晰、质量过关。

148
00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.950
And Catherine is so funny.
凯瑟琳真是太逗了。

149
00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.930
I can't believe we didn't see it for years.
真不敢相信我们这么多年都没发现。

150
00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:44.450
I know.
我知道。

151
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.470
Catherine in this picture.
照片里的凯瑟琳。

152
00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.910
Everyone looks cold.
大家看起来都很冷。

153
00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:48.970
Jenna, you look freezing.
珍娜，你看起来冻坏了。

154
00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.090
Kate Flannery is actually doing a thing with her face like, ooh.
凯特·弗兰纳里脸上的表情真的很有趣，像是在说“噢”。

155
00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:58.470
Like, but Catherine's face is completely covered by her hair.
但是凯瑟琳的脸完全被头发遮住了。

156
00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:58.790
Yeah.
是啊。

157
00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.250
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

158
00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.090
We'll put it in stories.
我们要把它发到快拍里。

159
00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:10.370
I also found in my digital clutter an email from our key second assistant director, Stephanie.
我还从我的数字杂物里翻出了一封我们关键的第二助理导演斯蒂芬妮发的邮件。

160
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:11.810
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

161
00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.030
I was just texting with Stephanie recently.
我最近刚和斯蒂芬妮发过短信。

162
00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:15.750
I love her.
我超喜欢她。

163
00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:21.450
Remember I told you I went to that birthday party where we discussed whether or not the birthday boy.
记得我跟你说过我去了那个生日派对，我们讨论了那个寿星到底是……

164
00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:21.950
Oh, yes.
噢，对。

165
00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:22.990
Was, right?
是吧？

166
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:23.370
Right.
没错。

167
00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:23.630
Okay.
好吧。

168
00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:24.450
Shower grower.
“缩水型”还是“充血型”。

169
00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:24.970
Right.
对。

170
00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:34.850
So I thought, oh, the morning after the birthday party, I'm going to send a fun text to all the ladies about, you know, some inside joke from the party.
所以我想，噢，生日派对后的第二天早上，我要给女士们发条有趣的短信，聊聊派对上的某个内部梗。

171
00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:40.630
So I send it to my friends, Michelle, Anne, and Steph.
于是我发给了我的朋友米歇尔、安妮和斯蒂芬。

172
00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.170
Oh, no.
噢，不。

173
00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.770
You texted the wrong Stephanie.
你发错斯蒂芬了。

174
00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:44.810
Texted the wrong Stephanie.
发错斯蒂芬了。

175
00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:56.770
And so Steph, our second AD, after a while of us not hearing from Steph, who was at the party, she texts back, hey, ladies, this sounds like a really fun party.
然后我们的第二助理导演斯蒂芬，在我们迟迟没收到那个参加派对的斯蒂芬回复后，她回信说：嘿，女士们，听起来是个很有趣的派对。

176
00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:57.070
Oh, no.
噢，不。

177
00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:01.130
But I think you mean this for a different Steph.
但我认为你们是发给另一个斯蒂芬了。

178
00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.230
Oh, no.
噢，不。

179
00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:07.050
But anyway, and then I was, like, texting her on the side and was like, how are you, though?
总之，后来我私下给她发短信说，不过你最近怎么样？

180
00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:08.730
All right.
好吧。

181
00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.510
So go ahead.
那继续吧。

182
00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.730
Steph sent an email.
斯蒂芬发了一封邮件。

183
00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:11.470
She did.
是的。

184
00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:13.930
It was to the entire cast, and here's what it said.
是发给全体演员的，内容如下。

185
00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.590
Hey, guys, I'm looking forward to the giant days we have coming up.
嘿，各位，我很期待接下来要拍的那些大场面。

186
00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.870
They should be a lot of fun.
应该会很有趣。

187
00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:25.170
I am trying to make the days run as smoothly as possible and want to alert you to our plans in advance.
我正努力让拍摄工作尽可能顺利进行，想提前告知大家我们的计划。

188
00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:32.050
Due to the nature of the set and the gorgeous views at the location, there is very little indoor space available to us.
由于片场的性质和拍摄地绝美的景色，我们可用的室内空间非常有限。

189
00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:37.930
We are planning to take advantage of the remoteness of the set, and we will see 360.
我们计划利用片场的偏远优势，进行360度全景拍摄。

190
00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.930
Oh, I remember this.
噢，我记得这个。

191
00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:40.410
Yeah.
是啊。

192
00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.690
So that meant we do not have any holding areas planned.
这意味着我们没有安排任何候场区。

193
00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:45.370
Yes.
是的。

194
00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.630
There were no trailers up there.
上面没有拖车。

195
00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.830
The trailers were down this long hill.
拖车都在长长山坡的下面。

196
00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:50.930
You had to take a van.
你必须坐面包车上去。

197
00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:59.390
So once we got ready at the bottom of the hill, you would take a van up to the top, and then you were just at this wedding.
所以一旦我们在山脚下准备好，就要坐面包车到山顶，然后你就直接在婚礼现场了。

198
00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:00.050
Right.
没错。

199
00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:06.770
Stephanie said, while we're shooting, there will be a small group of you who are working inside the house.
斯蒂芬说，拍摄期间，会有一小部分人在屋内工作。

200
00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.250
This is a hot set.
这是一个正在拍摄的场景。

201
00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.930
Please don't move anything around.
请不要移动任何东西。

202
00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:10.770
Yep.
没错。

203
00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.150
So we were inside that house, Dwight's farmhouse.
当时我们在那栋房子里，就是德怀特的农舍。

204
00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:20.710
The other thing I wanted to note is she wrote, there are 33 principal actors working today.
我还要提的一点是她写道，今天有33位主要演员在场。

205
00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.850
And 50 background performers.
还有50位背景演员。

206
00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:23.350
Yep.
没错。

207
00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.810
She wrote, we are preparing for rain.
她写道，我们正在为下雨做准备。

208
00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:30.250
And lastly, please be aware that there is no cell phone service.
最后，请注意这里没有手机信号。

209
00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.570
My cell phone has not been working at this location.
我的手机在这个位置一直没信号。

210
00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.810
Production is renting a temporary cell phone.
剧组租了一部临时手机。

211
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.110
Please try me by that or email me.
请试着打那个号码联系我，或者给我发邮件。

212
00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.390
We were really in the middle of nowhere.
我们真的是在荒郊野外。

213
00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:45.110
She included directions, which were very detailed.
她附上了路线指引，非常详细。

214
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.850
And I remember that drive, don't you, Jenna?
我记得那段车程，你记得吗，珍娜？

215
00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:48.070
Yeah.
记得。

216
00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.410
In the morning, it was full fog and miSt.
那天早上，到处都是浓雾和水汽。

217
00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:51.850
Yep.
没错。

218
00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:52.870
And we were driving.
我们当时正在开车。

219
00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:56.050
You would have thought we were sort of like in the highlands of Scotland.
你可能会以为我们是在苏格兰高地之类的什么地方。

220
00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.210
Yes, very much.
是的，非常像。

221
00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.350
That's a great comparison.
这个比喻太贴切了。

222
00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.950
We had to go through two different canyons.
我们不得不穿过两个不同的峡谷。

223
00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:09.250
Well, I think that these conditions actually lent themselves to a really, really fun final shoot experience.
嗯，我觉得这些条件实际上让这次最终拍摄体验变得非常、非常有意思。

224
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:15.690
It really reminded me of our early days on set when none of us had phones or working computers.
这真的让我想起了我们刚开始拍摄时的日子，那时我们谁都没有手机或能用的电脑。

225
00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.050
Yeah.
没错。

226
00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.790
And we just would sit on set.
我们只会坐在片场。

227
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.870
And hang out.
然后闲聊。

228
00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.130
And that's what we did when we shot this wedding.
拍这场婚礼时我们就是这么做的。

229
00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.530
We just hung out.
我们只是聚在一起闲聊。

230
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.750
And it was really fun.
真的很有趣。

231
00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.450
We hung out in parkas that had a piece of tape with our name on it.
我们穿着贴有写着名字的胶带的派克大衣聚在一起。

232
00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:28.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

233
00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.490
That's how we knew which parka was ours.
那就是我们辨认哪件大衣是自己衣服的方法。

234
00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.750
It was super cold.
当时超级冷。

235
00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:33.410
So cold.
冷极了。

236
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.670
And we just huddled up in that drafty house and talked and laughed.
我们就在那栋四面透风的房子里挤在一起，聊天大笑。

237
00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.070
And it was great.
感觉棒极了。

238
00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:39.870
All right.
好了。

239
00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.170
This is a big top of show, everybody.
各位，这是节目的重头戏。

240
00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.190
And I've got a big fast fact three.
我有一个非常重要的速递事实三。

241
00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:44.870
Yeah.
没错。

242
00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:50.690
Because we had a big guest star on this episode, Mr. Steve Carell.
因为这一集我们有一位重量级客串明星，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔先生。

243
00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.290
I still can't believe how they pulled this off.
我到现在都不敢相信他们是怎么做到的。

244
00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:55.470
I really can't.
真的不敢相信。

245
00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.690
We got a lot of fan mail about it.
我们收到了很多关于此事的粉丝来信。

246
00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.530
And I have a whole breakdown on how we made it work.
我有一个关于我们如何实现这一点的详细分析。

247
00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.890
Let's get into these fan questions.
让我们进入这些粉丝提问环节吧。

248
00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.430
Bailey E.
来自曼尼托巴省的贝利·E说，

249
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.330
from Manitoba said,
来自曼尼托巴省的贝利·E说，

250
00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:12.130
One of the scenes from The Office that never fails to make me cry is when Michael comes back to be Dwight's best man.
《办公室》里有一个场景每次看都会让我落泪，那就是迈克尔回来给德怀特当伴郎的时候。

251
00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.730
I've always wondered whose idea was it to have Steve Carell come back.
我一直很好奇，让史蒂夫·卡瑞尔回归是谁的主意。

252
00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.910
And was it a surprise to the cast?
这对演员阵容来说是个惊喜吗？

253
00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.670
And Megan Kaye from Tampa, Florida said,
来自佛罗里达州坦帕市的梅根·凯说：

254
00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:25.270
I'd love to know your lady's feelings on Steve coming back to the set.
我很想知道你夫人对史蒂夫回到片场有什么感想。

255
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:28.030
But in the opening credits, his name is not mentioned.
但在片头字幕里，并没有提到他的名字。

256
00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:31.130
So it was a huge surprise for viewers to see.
所以观众看到他出现时感到非常惊喜。

257
00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.790
I absolutely bawl every time I see it.
我每次看那一幕都会泪流满面。

258
00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.250
And I would love to know how it all came together.
我很想知道这一切是如何促成的。

259
00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:38.930
And Hugo S.
还有来自日本京都的雨果·S说：

260
00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.330
from Kyoto, Japan said,
让史蒂夫回归拍摄最后一集的过程是怎样的？

261
00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:44.190
What was the process in getting Steve to return for his final episode?
好吧，珍娜，你知道幕后发生的一切，而我们其他人却不知道。

262
00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:48.810
Well, Jenna, you know everything that was happening behind the scenes that the rest of us didn't know.
所以你必须分享一下。

263
00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.750
So you have to share.
好的。

264
00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:51.030
All right.
嗯，让史蒂夫回归是格雷格的主意。

265
00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.990
Well, it was Greg's idea to have Steve come back.
他很长一段时间以来一直都有这个想法。

266
00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.250
He had wanted that for a very long time.
他在第九季很早的时候就问过他了。

267
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.570
And he asked him pretty early in season nine.
但史蒂夫当时很犹豫。

268
00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.910
But Steve was reluctant.
他觉得迈克尔的故事已经真正结束了。

269
00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:05.210
He felt like Michael's story had really ended.
他不想再重新开启这个角色。

270
00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.310
He didn't want to open it back up again.
他尤其不想在两年后回来，让大结局这一集变成以他为中心。

271
00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:16.490
And he especially did not want to come back after two years and have this finale episode be about him.
史蒂夫真的觉得我的角色已经有了结局。

272
00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.910
Steve really felt like my character had his ending.
这是其他所有人的结局。

273
00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.770
This is everybody else's ending.
他不想喧宾夺主。

274
00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.770
And he didn't want to overshadow that.
嗯，他在这方面真的很谦逊。

275
00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.610
Well, he's very gracious that way.
是的。

276
00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:26.130
Yeah.
但后来格雷格想到了让最后一集变成德怀特和安吉拉婚礼的主意。

277
00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:32.770
But then Greg had the idea of the final episode being Dwight and Angela's wedding.
史蒂夫同意迈克尔会出席。

278
00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.230
And Steve agreed Michael would be there.
我相信这一点。

279
00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:37.710
I believe that.
我相信迈克尔会愿意为了德怀特和安吉拉出席婚礼。

280
00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.710
I believe Michael would want to be there for Dwight and Angela.
是的。

281
00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:41.370
Yeah.
这是一个有历史渊源支撑的创作理由，你懂的。

282
00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:46.530
It was a creative reason that was supported by history, you know?
我记得当时我和约翰在编剧室里，得知史蒂夫要回来的时候。

283
00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:52.890
So I remember being up in the writer's room with John when we found out that Steve was going to come back.
我们被要求严守秘密。

284
00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.730
And we were sworn to secrecy.
要做到这一点真的非常不容易。

285
00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.230
And this was, like, really epic to pull off.
我以前讲过这个故事。

286
00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.470
I've told this story before.
雷恩·威尔森转向我说，连安吉拉都不能告诉，珍娜。

287
00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.370
Rainn Wilson turned to me and he said, not even Angela, Jenna.
我说，好吧。

288
00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.190
I was like, okay.
真是太强势了。

289
00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:07.870
So aggressive.
我是说，他知道我什么都会告诉你。

290
00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.930
I mean, he knows I tell you everything.
我知道。

291
00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:10.490
I know.
不告诉你真的很难。

292
00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.770
It was really hard not to tell you.
因为，安吉，直到那天他出现在片场你才知道。

293
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:19.090
Because, Ang, you did not find out until he showed up on set that day.
哦，我记得那个确切的时刻。

294
00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.850
Oh, I know the exact moment.
我开车穿过了那两个峡谷。

295
00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:23.830
I had driven through the two canyons.
我走了那条土路。

296
00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.310
I had taken the dirt road.
我当时在荒郊野外的基地营地。

297
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.450
I was at our base camp in the middle of nowhere.
那里又冷又雾蒙蒙的。

298
00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.630
Where it was cold and foggy.
就在我快到发型和化妆间时，片场助理转向我说，哦，史蒂夫来了。

299
00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:38.370
And right as I was getting to hair and makeup, the set PA turned to me and said, oh, Steve is here.
我说，你在说什么呢？

300
00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.510
And I said, what are you talking about?
我一直很好奇，让史蒂夫·卡瑞尔回归是谁的主意。

301
00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.650
And at first I thought she meant Steve Burgess.
起初我还以为她说的是史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

302
00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.790
And she was like, Steve Carell is here.
她说，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔来了。

303
00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.010
I said, what?
我说，什么？

304
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.250
And I opened the door.
然后我打开了门。

305
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:52.990
And there he was.
他就站在那儿。

306
00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.790
He was sitting in hair and makeup.
他正坐在化妆间里做造型。

307
00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:58.370
And I just was like, Steve.
我当时就喊了声，史蒂夫。

308
00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.600
And I just hugged him.
然后直接给了他一个拥抱。

309
00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.680
And we were laughing.
我们都笑了。

310
00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:04.820
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

311
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.060
I was like so confused.
我当时整个人都懵了。

312
00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:09.200
And then we just got to chat in hair and makeup.
后来我们就坐在化妆间里聊天。

313
00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.960
And it was absolutely wonderful.
那感觉真是太棒了。

314
00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.780
I remember the vibe in the hair and makeup trailer.
我记得当时化妆拖车里的氛围。

315
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:15.340
When he was in there.
当他在里面的时候。

316
00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:16.220
Buzzing.
特别兴奋。

317
00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:16.560
Yeah.
是啊。

318
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.500
A body buzz.
全身都在兴奋。

319
00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:20.380
Everybody was like, it was a party.
每个人都觉得像是在开派对一样。

320
00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:20.800
Yeah.
没错。

321
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:27.640
Well, this was really crazy because Greg did not tell NBC that Steve was coming back.
这事儿真的很疯狂，因为格雷格没告诉NBC史蒂夫要回来。

322
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:33.200
Well, this is what I remember at the table read when all the NBC suits were there, all the executives.
我记得剧本围读的时候，NBC的所有高管都在场。

323
00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.140
In the script, it was Creed.
剧本里写的是克里德。

324
00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:37.660
Right?
对吧？

325
00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:38.260
Yeah.
是的。

326
00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.780
So that's the thing.
所以关键就在这儿。

327
00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:46.880
When you turn in a script, they use those script pages, those locations, those scenes to set a budget for your episode.
当你提交剧本时，他们会根据剧本页数、地点和场景来设定单集预算。

328
00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:53.500
And so they had a scene at our table read between Dwight and Jim.
所以在剧本围读时，我们确实有一场德怀特和吉姆的戏。

329
00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.380
But it wasn't the scene that ended up in the show.
但那并不是最终出现在剧里的那一幕。

330
00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.480
But there was a scene.
不过确实有那么一场戏。

331
00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:03.420
It was a placeholder of Jim helping Dwight right before it's time to go to the wedding.
那是个占位符，讲的是吉姆在去婚礼前帮德怀特。

332
00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:08.680
Same number of lines, same page count as the real scene with Steve.
台词数量和页数都和后来史蒂夫拍的那场戏一模一样。

333
00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:17.380
And then later, Michael has a talking head where he says, oh, it's like all my kids grew up and they got married.
后来迈克尔有个采访镜头，他说，哦，就像我的孩子们都长大了，结婚了一样。

334
00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:18.940
Creed read that.
那是克里德读的。

335
00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:19.600
Yes.
没错。

336
00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.340
At the table read, Creed read it.
在围读会上，是克里德读的。

337
00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:22.720
It was a Creed talking head.
那本来是克里德的采访镜头。

338
00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.700
It got a laugh.
还挺好笑的。

339
00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:24.200
It did.
确实。

340
00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.040
So no one at NBC knew.
所以NBC那边没人知道。

341
00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:27.580
No.
没有。

342
00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:35.760
And Steve Burgess told me that NBC has a rule that nobody can be filmed for the show without a signed contract.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，NBC有个规定，没签合同的人不能参与拍摄。

343
00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:44.360
So in order to follow the rules and still keep the secret, Steve Carell signed a contract to do the show for this episode.
所以为了遵守规定又保密，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔签了这一集的出演合同。

344
00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:50.600
But Steve Burgess kept it locked in his desk drawer until the day the show aired.
但史蒂夫·伯吉斯把合同锁在办公桌抽屉里，直到剧集播出那天。

345
00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:51.760
Steve Burgess?
史蒂夫·伯吉斯？

346
00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.300
So he could be like, no, no, no.
这样他就能说，不不不。

347
00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:54.200
Look at the date.
你看日期。

348
00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.260
I had a contract.
我有合同的。

349
00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.500
I just forgot to hand it in.
只是忘了交上去而已。

350
00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.340
This is some serious maneuvering.
这操作真是太硬核了。

351
00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.440
There's more, lady.
还没完呢，女士。

352
00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:08.440
So usually every day after you shoot, you send those tapes into the studio.
通常每天拍摄结束后，你们会把录影带送到制片厂。

353
00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:09.600
They're called the dailies.
那叫样片。

354
00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:09.940
Right.
没错。

355
00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.780
For them to review if they have something they didn't like, they want to take out.
他们要审阅，如果有什么不满意的地方，他们会想删掉。

356
00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:14.200
Yep.
是啊。

357
00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:14.760
Yada, yada.
诸如此类的。

358
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.840
They didn't send Steve scenes.
他们没把史蒂夫的戏份发过去。

359
00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.800
They kept them locked up somewhere else.
他们把那些素材锁在别的地方了。

360
00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:28.660
And then Dave Rogers did a cut of the episode because the network has to give notes, sent a Steve-less version.
然后戴夫·罗杰斯剪辑了那一集，因为电视台需要审阅并提出意见，所以他发过去的是没有史蒂夫的版本。

361
00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:34.160
So there's a lot of people in cahoots here to keep Steve's appearance a secret.
所以很多人都在暗中串通，为了保守史蒂夫回归的秘密。

362
00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.500
And I know Greg had a specific reason.
而且我知道格雷格有特别的原因。

363
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:37.320
Share it, Jenna.
说出来吧，珍娜。

364
00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:47.460
He was afraid that if he turned in any footage of Steve Carell on the show before it aired, that NBC would make promos out of it and ruin the surprise.
他担心如果他在节目播出前提交任何史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的镜头，NBC电视台就会拿去剪成预告片，从而破坏惊喜。

365
00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.540
Oh, they would want the ratings for sure.
噢，他们肯定会想利用这个来拉收视率。

366
00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:49.820
Right?
对吧？

367
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:50.280
Yeah.
是啊。

368
00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.600
And then it wouldn't have been a surprise.
那样的话，惊喜感就没了。

369
00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.500
I get that.
我明白。

370
00:17:53.500 --> 00:18:00.480
So finally, we had our final cut, the version that we had to turn in to the network with Steve.
所以最后，我们完成了最终剪辑版，也就是必须提交给电视台的那个包含史蒂夫的版本。

371
00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:01.340
With Steve.
有史蒂夫的版本。

372
00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.160
But we weren't turning it in.
但我们一直没交。

373
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:09.860
And I guess NBC finally put their foot down and said, we will not air something that no one here has seen.
我猜NBC最后强硬起来，说如果他们没看过，就绝不会播出。

374
00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:20.280
So Greg and Steve Burgess and Dave Rogers and Claire Scanlon said, you can come stand in our edit bay and watch it.
于是格雷格、史蒂夫·伯吉斯、戴夫·罗杰斯和克莱尔·斯坎伦就说，你们可以来我们的剪辑室现场看。

375
00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.900
But did that piss him off?
但这让他们生气了吗？

376
00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.640
I'm sure none of this never happens.
我敢说这种事以前从没发生过。

377
00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:30.000
Steve Burgess was like, I'll never work in this town again.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯当时说，我以后再也没法在这个圈子里混了。

378
00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.700
And Greg was like, it'll be fine.
格雷格则说，没事的。

379
00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:41.780
So Steve Burgess said, you should have seen their faces as they're standing in the edit bay the day before the episode was going to air.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，你真该看看他们在剧集播出前一天站在剪辑室里的表情。

380
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:45.940
Were they so grumpy that they had to come to our studios and stand in that edit bay?
他们是因为不得不亲自跑到我们的工作室站在剪辑室里看，所以才那么不高兴吗？

381
00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:53.140
He said, when they saw Steve come on, there was this mixture of them being like so pissed and so excited.
他说，当他们看到史蒂夫出现时，那种表情混合了愤怒和兴奋。

382
00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:59.460
And Dave Rogers said that they waited until 9 a.m.
戴夫·罗杰斯说，他们一直等到播出当天早上9点

383
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:03.260
the day the finale aired to actually hand over the episode.
才真正把那一集交出去。

384
00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.040
Wow.
哇。

385
00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.080
Is that the greatest kept secret?
这难道不是最伟大的秘密吗？

386
00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.280
I mean, yeah.
我是说，确实。

387
00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.740
It's got to be one of the best kept secrets in television.
这绝对是电视史上保密工作做得最好的事件之一。

388
00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.880
I would have been so stressed.
我要是当事人肯定压力山大。

389
00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:15.740
I would have been horrible.
我肯定会表现得很糟糕。

390
00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:16.540
But also.
但话说回来。

391
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.540
I'm so glad I didn't know.
我很高兴我当时不知道。

392
00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.320
I'm so glad.
真的很高兴。

393
00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.720
I was so excited when you finally knew.
当你最终知道的时候，我特别兴奋。

394
00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.220
I was like, ah.
我当时心想，啊。

395
00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:25.860
But I mean, even that, like we still had to keep the secret till it aired.
但我的意思是，即便如此，我们还是得保守秘密直到播出。

396
00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:26.240
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

397
00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:30.560
We did so much press and everybody asked us if Steve was coming back.
我们做了很多媒体采访，每个人都问我们史蒂夫会不会回来。

398
00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:35.220
David Letterman asked John Krasinski if Steve was coming back and John lied to him.
大卫·莱特曼问约翰·卡拉辛斯基史蒂夫会不会回来，约翰对他撒了谎。

399
00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:35.500
Yeah.
是啊。

400
00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:36.480
Lied to his face.
当面撒谎。

401
00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:37.740
Lied to David Letterman.
对大卫·莱特曼撒了谎。

402
00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:38.160
David Letterman.
大卫·莱特曼。

403
00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:41.940
And no, we were asked tons of questions about the finale.
不，当时有人问了我们一大堆关于大结局的问题。

404
00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:48.100
And Greg sent out an email and was like, I need you all to come together and not say a word on this.
格雷格发了一封邮件，大意是：我需要你们所有人统一口径，对此只字不提。

405
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.440
And we didn't.
我们确实做到了。

406
00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:50.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

407
00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.140
All right.
好吧。

408
00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.960
Well, like I said, that's a very long top of show.
如我所说，节目开场确实很长。

409
00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.600
But there was a lot to cover.
但要讲的内容实在太多了。

410
00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.000
There was and there still is a lot to cover.
确实如此，而且现在要讲的依然很多。

411
00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.980
Maybe we should take a break.
也许我们该休息一下了。

412
00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.880
And when we come back, I brought some show and tell iteMs.
等回来之后，我带了一些展示用的纪念品。

413
00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:03.960
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

414
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:19.400
We are back and we are starting with finale show and tell.
我们回来了，现在开始大结局的展示环节。

415
00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.920
Should I be getting my camera out?
我是不是该把相机拿出来？

416
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:22.680
Maybe.
也许吧。

417
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.600
Sam, Cassie, guess what I brought today?
山姆，卡西，猜猜我今天带了什么？

418
00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:33.180
I brought my finale part one and two script.
我带了我的大结局第一部分和第二部分的剧本。

419
00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:40.180
It's the shooting draft that we were given at the table read and I had the entire cast sign it.
这是我们在剧本围读会上拿到的拍摄底稿，我还让全体演员在上面签了名。

420
00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:40.420
Oh, like a new book.
噢，就像一本新书一样。

421
00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.260
Wow.
哇。

422
00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.160
Wow.
哇。

423
00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.500
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

424
00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.380
Isn't that cool?
是不是很酷？

425
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:45.640
You should frame that.
你应该把它装裱起来。

426
00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.200
I know, right?
对吧？

427
00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.700
This is what I found as I went through my bins of stuff.
这是我在翻找旧物箱时发现的。

428
00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.480
I had a bin called Trailer Finale.
我有一个箱子专门标着“剧组大结局”。

429
00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:54.380
Oh.
噢。

430
00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:54.960
Yeah.
没错。

431
00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.360
What's next?
接下来是什么？

432
00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.080
What's next is?
接下来是？

433
00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:03.520
I'm going to share one more here and then I have two more that I'll share later in the episode.
我先分享这一件，剩下的两件我会在节目后面再分享。

434
00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:03.920
Okay.
好的。

435
00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:08.620
So here's the thing I want you all to know about Jenna and I's friendship.
关于我和珍娜的友谊，有件事我想让你们都知道。

436
00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:21.420
Jenna is a card giver and it's something I love about her and I have saved all the cards you've ever given me and you always give me a card that marks a big moment.
珍娜是个喜欢送贺卡的人，这是我爱她的一点，我保存了你送给我的每一张贺卡，你总是在重要的时刻送我贺卡。

437
00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.760
I'm horrible at giving cards.
我送贺卡真的很糟糕。

438
00:21:24.020 --> 00:21:25.500
I love to make a gift.
我喜欢亲手制作礼物。

439
00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.440
I love to buy a gift.
我喜欢购买礼物。

440
00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:32.380
But in our friendship, you give cards and I brought a few.
但在我们的友谊中，你负责送贺卡，我也带了几张过来。

441
00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:36.740
First of all, you gave me a card when we started this podcaSt.
首先，我们开始做这个播客时，你送了我一张贺卡。

442
00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:37.920
I did?
我有吗？

443
00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:38.520
Yes.
有的。

444
00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:39.700
I have no memory of this.
我完全没印象了。

445
00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:47.320
And you wrote in it, you said, I have no idea if anyone is going to listen to us, but I'm just happy I get to do this with my best friend.
你在上面写道：我不知道会不会有人听我们的节目，但我很高兴能和最好的朋友一起做这件事。

446
00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:48.920
That's such a nice card.
那真是一张很棒的贺卡。

447
00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:51.600
You're a nice card writer.
你是个很会写贺卡的人。

448
00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:52.700
Okay.
好的。

449
00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:59.600
Then I saved the card you gave me at the end of the show when we wrapped the office.
然后我还保存了《办公室》杀青时你送我的那张贺卡。

450
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:00.880
Here it is.
就在这儿。

451
00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:04.100
This is a picture of me coming over the partition.
这张照片是我从隔板后面探出头来的样子。

452
00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:05.800
We shared this in our book.
我们在书里分享过这张照片。

453
00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:11.160
This is how you saw me for nine years, just my little tiny head coming over the partition.
这就是你们九年来看到我的样子，只有我的小脑袋从隔板后面露出来。

454
00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:12.260
It's how I met you.
我就是这样认识你们的。

455
00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:13.120
That's right.
没错。

456
00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:15.300
And you wrote this.
而且你写了这个。

457
00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.100
And if it's all right, I'm going to read it.
如果可以的话，我想把它读出来。

458
00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:17.640
Okay.
好的。

459
00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.140
Angela, it's true what Steve said.
安吉拉，史蒂夫说的是真的。

460
00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:23.600
No matter what happens with the show, I am so happy to have met you.
无论这部剧未来如何，我都很高兴能遇见你。

461
00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:27.600
You have quickly become one of my closest girlfriends, and it is such a gift.
你很快就成了我最亲密的闺蜜之一，这真是一份礼物。

462
00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:32.520
At my age, I don't always expect to meet a new person who I could bond with so easily.
到了我这个年纪，我没指望还能这么容易地结识一位能交心的新朋友。

463
00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:34.600
You are the funniest woman I know.
你是我认识的最风趣的女性。

464
00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:36.060
Now it's in writing.
现在这可是白纸黑字写下来了。

465
00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:38.860
And I just love our time together.
我真的很喜欢我们在一起的时光。

466
00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:40.680
BFF, Jenna.
永远的好朋友，珍娜。

467
00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:41.400
Aww.
噢。

468
00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.440
Well, you are the funniest woman I know.
好吧，你也是我认识的最风趣的女性。

469
00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:46.660
You put it in writing.
你把它写下来了。

470
00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:47.640
It's in writing.
写下来了。

471
00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:49.360
It's been written down.
已经记录在案了。

472
00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:58.540
Anyway, it's one of the things I absolutely love about our friendship is you are great at giving cards, and I save them, and they mean so much to me.
总之，我非常喜欢我们友谊的一点就是，你很擅长送贺卡，而我都会留着，它们对我意义重大。

473
00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:01.980
Well, I guess I'm good at giving cards, and you're good at saving things.
好吧，我想我擅长送贺卡，而你擅长保存东西。

474
00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:03.360
This is true.
确实如此。

475
00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:06.940
And that's one of the things I love about you.
这也是我喜欢你的原因之一。

476
00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:09.700
Well, that ends our show and tell right now.
好了，我们的展示环节就到此为止。

477
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:14.580
Oh, I also want you guys to know I have tons of pictures from this episode.
噢，我还想让大家知道，我这集有很多照片。

478
00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:16.020
I brought my camera.
我带了相机。

479
00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:17.660
I'll be sharing them in stories.
我会把它们分享在快拍里。

480
00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:26.720
But also, Steve Burgess sent us so many fantastic behind-the-scenes pictures from this episode, just like a treasure of pictures.
另外，史蒂夫·伯吉斯也给我们发了很多这集精彩的幕后照片，简直是一座照片宝库。

481
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:27.500
He did.
他确实发了。

482
00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:29.300
We'll be putting those in stories as well.
我们也会把那些照片发到快拍里。

483
00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:30.680
Well, let's get started.
好了，我们开始吧。

484
00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:31.720
Here we are.
我们到了。

485
00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:33.060
We're at Shroot FarMs.
我们在施鲁特农场。

486
00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:37.380
The wedding guests are arriving, and they're bringing cats as gifts.
婚礼宾客陆续抵达，他们还带着猫作为礼物。

487
00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:38.500
I loved it.
我太喜欢这个了。

488
00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.120
Here's how this scene was described in the shooting draft.
以下是拍摄剧本中对这一场景的描述。

489
00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:43.340
Kevin puts his cat in the gift basket.
凯文把他的猫放进礼品篮里。

490
00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:46.180
Behind him, Pete has a cat for her, too.
在他身后，皮特也为她准备了一只猫。

491
00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:50.520
Behind him, Creed, wearing his beard, puts a cat in the basket.
在他身后，克里德戴着胡子，把一只猫放进篮子里。

492
00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:53.220
The cats keep escaping from the basket.
猫不断地从篮子里逃出来。

493
00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.020
A caterer keeps scooping them up and putting them back in the basket.
一名餐饮服务员不停地把它们捞起来放回篮子里。

494
00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.080
Meredith shows up with a cat.
梅雷迪思带着一只猫出现了。

495
00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:01.120
She looks gorgeous and classy.
她看起来既华丽又优雅。

496
00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:02.180
Oh.
噢。

497
00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:02.920
Hmm.
嗯。

498
00:24:03.300 --> 00:24:06.400
Well, that's a little bit more than what we see play out in the scene.
好吧，这比我们在剧中看到的场景要多一点。

499
00:24:06.400 --> 00:24:10.920
In this scene, we do see Dakota introduce herself to Creed.
在这一幕中，我们确实看到了达科塔向克里德做自我介绍。

500
00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:12.240
This is when we learn her name.
我们就是在这时知道她名字的。

501
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:12.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

502
00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.360
Creed says he's Jeff Bermotto.
克里德说他叫杰夫·伯莫托。

503
00:24:15.860 --> 00:24:17.800
He sells ceramic tile out of Newark.
他在纽瓦克卖瓷砖。

504
00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:19.600
Yeah, he has a wife named Catherine.
对，他有个妻子叫凯瑟琳。

505
00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:20.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

506
00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:22.680
He can show you his social security card if it helps.
如果需要的话，他可以给你看他的社保卡。

507
00:24:23.180 --> 00:24:24.820
Dakota's like, okay, whatever.
达科塔当时就觉得，好吧，随你便。

508
00:24:25.180 --> 00:24:32.020
I would like to point out that our writers, Jen Salata and Graham Wagner, are reprising their roles as the Shroot family members.
我想指出，我们的编剧简·萨拉塔和格雷厄姆·瓦格纳在这一幕中客串了施鲁特家族的成员。

509
00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:34.300
They're arriving for the wedding during this scene as well.
他们也是在这一幕中抵达婚礼现场的。

510
00:24:34.300 --> 00:24:38.640
Now we see Kelly and Ravi, they're in their seats for Dwight and Angela's wedding.
现在我们看到凯莉和拉维，他们已经在德怀特和安吉拉的婚礼上入座了。

511
00:24:38.800 --> 00:24:41.720
When Ryan approaches, he's got a baby strapped to his cheSt.
当瑞安走过来时，他的胸前绑着一个婴儿。

512
00:24:41.980 --> 00:24:43.760
I have a show-and-tell moment for here.
我这里有个展示环节。

513
00:24:43.920 --> 00:24:44.520
Oh, already?
哦，这么快？

514
00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:45.320
Already.
没错。

515
00:24:45.540 --> 00:24:46.140
What is it?
是什么？

516
00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:48.580
Kelly and Ravi are holding the wedding program.
凯莉和拉维手里拿着婚礼流程单。

517
00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:49.260
Oh.
哦。

518
00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:50.240
And I kept one.
我留了一份。

519
00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:52.580
Phil Shea gave it to me, and I still have it.
菲尔·谢给了我一份，我一直留着。

520
00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:53.400
Look, Sam.
看，萨姆。

521
00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:53.920
Cassie.
卡西。

522
00:24:54.080 --> 00:24:55.200
I have the wedding program.
我有婚礼流程单。

523
00:24:55.700 --> 00:24:56.140
Wow.
哇。

524
00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:58.700
That is a good prop to have.
那真是个不错的道具。

525
00:24:58.700 --> 00:25:08.180
We share this in our book as well, but it says that Angela and Dwight's wedding is taking place on Saturday, the 14th of June at 3 o'clock in the afternoon.
我们在书里也分享过这个，上面写着安吉拉和德怀特的婚礼将于6月14日星期六下午3点举行。

526
00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:09.120
Okay.
好的。

527
00:25:09.720 --> 00:25:15.640
It says that her co-maids of honor are Pam Halpert, Meredith Palmer, Phyllis Vance, and Rachel Martin.
上面写着她的伴娘团是帕姆·哈珀特、梅雷迪斯·帕尔默、菲利斯·万斯和瑞秋·马丁。

528
00:25:16.140 --> 00:25:18.680
So that was actually a plot point that got cut out.
所以那其实是一个被删减的情节。

529
00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:23.620
It's why we are all throwing your bachelorette party, because we are your co-maids of honor.
这就是为什么我们都在为你举办单身派对，因为我们都是你的伴娘。

530
00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:31.720
And the groomsmen are Andy Bernard, Oscar Martinez, Zeke Schrute, and Mo Schrute, Bestest Minch, Jim Halpert.
伴郎是安迪·伯纳德、奥斯卡·马丁内斯、齐克·施鲁特、莫·施鲁特、最佳男傧相明奇和吉姆·哈珀特。

531
00:25:32.300 --> 00:25:34.140
Angela does not have a maid of honor.
安吉拉没有首席伴娘。

532
00:25:34.680 --> 00:25:34.880
Oh.
哦。

533
00:25:35.320 --> 00:25:35.920
Interesting.
有意思。

534
00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:38.800
It also lists Dwight and Angela's parents.
上面还列出了德怀特和安吉拉父母的名字。

535
00:25:39.340 --> 00:25:40.680
Do you want to hear their names?
你想听听他们的名字吗？

536
00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:41.280
Sure.
好啊。

537
00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:43.760
We're going to see Angela's parents later.
我们稍后会见到安吉拉的父母。

538
00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:48.040
Angela's mother and father are Anne Marie Martin and Sean T.
安吉拉的母亲和父亲是安妮·玛丽·马丁和肖恩·T。

539
00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:48.500
Martin.
马丁。

540
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:49.240
Okay.
好的。

541
00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:55.080
Dwight's mother and father are Hedda Mannheim Schrute and Dwight Schrute Sr.
德怀特的母亲和父亲是海达·曼海姆·施鲁特和老德怀特·施鲁特。

542
00:25:55.740 --> 00:25:58.440
There was a flower girl, Cece Halpert.
花童是西西·哈珀特。

543
00:25:58.800 --> 00:25:59.060
Yes.
是的。

544
00:25:59.480 --> 00:26:02.220
And the ring bearer was Philip Halstead Lipton.
而送戒童是菲利普·霍尔斯特德·利普顿。

545
00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:03.480
There you go.
就是这样。

546
00:26:03.660 --> 00:26:05.060
Dwight and Angela's wedding program.
德怀特和安吉拉的婚礼流程单。

547
00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:09.280
Well, that was all done by the late, great Phil Shea.
嗯，这一切都是已故的伟大道具师菲尔·谢完成的。

548
00:26:09.540 --> 00:26:09.700
Yep.
没错。

549
00:26:10.420 --> 00:26:12.700
Kelly's going to ask Ryan if he's a manny.
凯莉会问瑞安他是不是个男保姆。

550
00:26:13.180 --> 00:26:15.740
And Ryan's like, no, this little guy's mine.
而瑞安会说，不，这个小家伙是我的。

551
00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:16.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

552
00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:21.100
I would like to give the cutest smile in the finale, Dundee, in this scene.
我想在这一幕的结局里，给邓迪奖一个最可爱的微笑。

553
00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:22.680
Is it to the little baby?
是对那个小宝宝吗？

554
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:23.520
Yes.
是的。

555
00:26:23.780 --> 00:26:24.980
What a cutie.
真是个小可爱。

556
00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:29.220
Steve Burgess said we had three pairs of twins.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说我们有三对双胞胎。

557
00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:30.220
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

558
00:26:30.340 --> 00:26:31.520
As possible babies.
作为候选宝宝。

559
00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:38.580
But there was one baby, and he unfortunately did not know the name, that was like superior to all the babies.
但其中有一个宝宝——他很遗憾不知道名字——比所有其他宝宝都更出色。

560
00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:41.740
And that's the one you see there winning the smiley Dundee.
那就是你在那儿看到的赢得微笑邓迪奖的那个宝宝。

561
00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:42.680
What a cutie.
真是个小可爱。

562
00:26:43.620 --> 00:26:48.560
Oh, I want to give a guest star shout out to Sentil Ramamurthy, who played Ravi.
噢，我想特别感谢一下客串明星森德希·拉玛莫西，他饰演了拉维。

563
00:26:48.800 --> 00:26:49.440
He's back.
他回来了。

564
00:26:49.640 --> 00:26:50.220
He's amazing.
他太棒了。

565
00:26:50.420 --> 00:26:51.220
He's so good.
他演得真好。

566
00:26:51.480 --> 00:26:51.980
He's so good.
他演得真好。

567
00:26:52.320 --> 00:26:59.480
Well, Kelly thinks Ryan's baby is adorable, especially compared to some of the uggos that Ravi treats as a pediatrician.
嗯，凯莉觉得瑞安的宝宝很可爱，尤其是和拉维作为儿科医生治疗的一些丑宝宝相比。

568
00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:02.180
Ravi says they're called premature, sweetie.
拉维说那些叫早产儿，亲爱的。

569
00:27:02.480 --> 00:27:02.740
Right.
没错。

570
00:27:02.860 --> 00:27:04.300
It's good to see you again, Ryan.
很高兴再次见到你，瑞安。

571
00:27:04.740 --> 00:27:05.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

572
00:27:05.120 --> 00:27:13.360
And, you know, from the minute Ryan sits down, we see a look on Kelly's face, and I think we all know what's going to happen.
而且，你知道，从瑞安坐下的那一刻起，我们就能从凯莉的表情看出来，我想我们都知道接下来会发生什么。

573
00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:15.120
Oh, you know it.
噢，你懂的。

574
00:27:15.320 --> 00:27:16.180
You know it.
你懂的。

575
00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:18.480
We are now in the bridal dressing room.
我们现在在新娘化妆间。

576
00:27:18.620 --> 00:27:22.240
Pam, Phyllis, and Angela's sister, Rachel, are helping Angela get ready.
帕姆、菲利斯和安吉拉的妹妹瑞秋正在帮安吉拉做准备。

577
00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:24.560
Angela is really struggling in her heels.
安吉拉穿着高跟鞋真的很吃力。

578
00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:28.620
I guess, you know, spending hours in a trunk, her legs are all sore.
我想，你知道，在后备箱里待了几个小时，她的腿都酸了。

579
00:27:28.800 --> 00:27:30.900
She can't really stand up or walk.
她根本站不起来，也没法走路。

580
00:27:30.980 --> 00:27:31.220
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

581
00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:33.020
And she's really mad at Phyllis about it.
而且她为此对菲利斯非常生气。

582
00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:35.940
This is the first time we see Angela in her wedding dress.
这是我们第一次看到安吉拉穿婚纱的样子。

583
00:27:36.060 --> 00:27:37.140
Yes, that's true.
是的，没错。

584
00:27:37.580 --> 00:27:41.480
We've mentioned this before, but it looks very similar to Phyllis' wedding dress.
我们之前提过，但这看起来和菲利斯的婚纱很像。

585
00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:44.680
It's a strapless dress with a lace jacket.
那是一件带蕾丝外套的抹胸裙。

586
00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:47.200
Angela's hair is half up, half down.
安吉拉的发型是半扎半披的。

587
00:27:47.960 --> 00:27:49.920
This was a very fun wardrobe fitting.
这是一次非常有趣的服装试穿。

588
00:27:50.100 --> 00:27:51.480
I still have the pictures from it.
我至今还留着当时的照片。

589
00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:57.300
And, of course, Kim Ferry wanted to do a little classic mini bun swoop.
当然，金·费里想做一个经典的迷你发髻造型。

590
00:27:57.360 --> 00:28:00.920
So her hair is half up, half down with a cute little knot.
所以她的头发是半扎半披的，还带了一个可爱的小发结。

591
00:28:01.160 --> 00:28:01.680
I saw it.
我看到了。

592
00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:02.280
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

593
00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:05.060
It was a great detail and a call back to the character.
这是一个很棒的细节，也是对角色过往的回应。

594
00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:05.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

595
00:28:06.360 --> 00:28:12.160
Well, Phyllis is going to tell Angela, I'm going to get you to the altar and you can take
嗯，菲利斯要告诉安吉拉，我会把你送到祭坛前，你可以把这句话

596
00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:13.060
that to the bank.
当成金科玉律。

597
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:13.880
Yes.
是的。

598
00:28:14.080 --> 00:28:18.620
I have such a clear memory of Phyllis saying you can take that to the bank.
我清楚地记得菲利斯说你可以把这句话当成金科玉律。

599
00:28:18.820 --> 00:28:22.500
She was so proud that she was going to take care of things.
她为自己能把事情处理好感到非常自豪。

600
00:28:22.620 --> 00:28:24.520
And it was a really sweet moment.
那真是一个非常温馨的时刻。

601
00:28:25.140 --> 00:28:28.140
Well, now we're going to go to the groom's dressing room.
好了，现在我们要去新郎的更衣室了。

602
00:28:29.060 --> 00:28:30.000
Dwight's getting ready.
德怀特正在准备。

603
00:28:30.380 --> 00:28:31.360
Jim is helping him.
吉姆在帮他。

604
00:28:31.520 --> 00:28:33.920
We have a call back, another little Easter egg.
我们有个呼应，又一个小彩蛋。

605
00:28:34.580 --> 00:28:37.680
Dwight does his air guitar to pump himself up.
德怀特弹空气吉他来给自己打气。

606
00:28:37.820 --> 00:28:38.540
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

607
00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:39.460
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

608
00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:40.880
He's like, I was born ready.
他就像是说，我天生就准备好了。

609
00:28:40.920 --> 00:28:45.380
And it's that call back to what he would do in the stairwell before there was a big meeting.
这呼应了他以前在重大会议前在楼梯间做的事情。

610
00:28:45.680 --> 00:28:47.340
Well, Jim's going to give him some news.
好吧，吉姆要告诉他一个消息。

611
00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:53.100
He says, I just found out that I cannot be your bestest mensch because the bestest mensch
他说，我刚发现我不能当你的最佳伴郎了，因为最佳伴郎

612
00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:54.860
has to be older than the groom.
必须比新郎年纪大。

613
00:28:55.220 --> 00:28:56.340
What are we going to do?
我们该怎么办？

614
00:28:56.920 --> 00:28:59.000
Rain and John are really funny in this scene.
雷恩和约翰在这场戏里真的很有趣。

615
00:28:59.180 --> 00:28:59.640
They are.
确实。

616
00:28:59.860 --> 00:29:03.140
When John as Jim is like, I'm significantly younger than you.
当约翰饰演的吉姆说，我比你年轻得多时。

617
00:29:03.140 --> 00:29:05.920
And Dwight's like, I don't know if I'd say that significantly.
德怀特说，我不知道能不能说年轻得多。

618
00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:07.380
Maybe a teeny bit.
也许就一点点。

619
00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:12.200
That's when Jim says, I just really wish there was something I could do.
就在那时吉姆说，我真希望我能做点什么。

620
00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:14.840
And then his eyes kind of look off.
然后他的眼神看向了别处。

621
00:29:15.260 --> 00:29:16.880
The camera pans over.
摄像机平移过去。

622
00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:18.060
And guess who's there?
你猜谁在那儿？

623
00:29:18.540 --> 00:29:19.520
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特。

624
00:29:19.720 --> 00:29:20.560
I know.
我知道。

625
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:23.260
And Dwight says, Michael, I can't believe you came.
德怀特说，迈克尔，真不敢相信你来了。

626
00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:25.640
And Michael says, that's what she said.
迈克尔说，那是她说的。

627
00:29:25.900 --> 00:29:29.940
And that's the last time Steve Carell ever said, that's what she said.
那是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔最后一次说那句“那是她说的”。

628
00:29:29.940 --> 00:29:31.920
He has not said it since.
从那以后他就没再说过。

629
00:29:32.060 --> 00:29:33.160
That was the last time.
那是最后一次。

630
00:29:33.520 --> 00:29:34.700
Well, it was perfect.
嗯，太完美了。

631
00:29:34.980 --> 00:29:37.700
If that's going to be your last one, that's a great way to go.
如果那将是你的最后一句，那真是个完美的谢幕。

632
00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:38.360
Perfect.
完美。

633
00:29:38.820 --> 00:29:41.160
Jim says, best prank ever.
吉姆说，史上最棒的恶作剧。

634
00:29:41.700 --> 00:29:43.880
Now it's time for the wedding ceremony.
现在是婚礼仪式的时间了。

635
00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:45.720
The processional begins.
入场式开始了。

636
00:29:45.800 --> 00:29:52.520
And Phyllis is carrying Angela on her back while a string quartet plays Sweet Child of Mine.
菲利斯背着安吉拉走进来，弦乐四重奏正在演奏《Sweet Child of Mine》。

637
00:29:53.040 --> 00:29:56.700
Steve Burgess said Sweet Child of Mine was very difficult to clear.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说《Sweet Child of Mine》的版权非常难搞定。

638
00:29:56.700 --> 00:29:58.640
This is the song the writers wanted.
这是编剧们想要的歌。

639
00:29:58.980 --> 00:30:03.840
But since we did not use Guns N' Roses singing it, it was allowed.
但因为我们没有使用枪花乐队的原唱版本，所以是被允许的。

640
00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:06.400
But it still cost $50,000.
但它依然花费了五万美元。

641
00:30:07.020 --> 00:30:07.580
Damn.
天哪。

642
00:30:08.140 --> 00:30:10.020
Just to have a string quartet play it.
仅仅是为了让弦乐四重奏演奏它。

643
00:30:10.340 --> 00:30:11.260
Popular song.
流行歌曲啊。

644
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:11.880
Wow.
哇。

645
00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:18.540
I have to think that Angela and Dwight had a few arguments over the song choices for the wedding.
我觉得安吉拉和德怀特在婚礼选曲上肯定吵过几次架。

646
00:30:18.740 --> 00:30:19.300
You think so?
你这么觉得？

647
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:24.900
I don't think Angela would have picked Sweet Child of Mine as her entrance.
我不觉得安吉拉会选《Sweet Child of Mine》作为她的入场曲。

648
00:30:24.900 --> 00:30:27.560
We got a fan question from Jenna F.
我们收到了来自洛杉矶的珍娜·F的一位粉丝提问，她说，

649
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:29.400
in Los Angeles who said,
在洛杉矶，她说，

650
00:30:29.540 --> 00:30:37.740
This seemingly simple bit of Phyllis carrying you down the aisle actually required a pretty elaborate set of circumstances to pull off.
菲利斯背着你走过过道的这个看似简单的片段，实际上需要相当复杂的条件才能完成。

651
00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:40.540
You wrote about it in your book, The Office BFFs.
你在你的书《办公室死党》里写过这件事。

652
00:30:40.620 --> 00:30:42.840
But Angela, will you tell the story on the podcast?
但是安吉拉，你愿意在播客里讲讲这个故事吗？

653
00:30:43.280 --> 00:30:45.160
Thank you, Jenna F., for writing in.
谢谢你，珍娜·F，来信分享。

654
00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:48.920
You've been a loyal writer, commentator on this podcaSt.
你一直是这个播客忠实的写信人和评论者。

655
00:30:49.660 --> 00:30:52.820
Well, this is how it was described in the shooting draft.
嗯，拍摄剧本里是这样描述的。

656
00:30:53.440 --> 00:31:00.420
Dwight stands in a shallow grave with an empty one next to him, beside Jim and Andy and the ushers under a bower of flowers.
德怀特站在一个浅坑里，旁边还有一个空坑，吉姆、安迪和引座员站在花架下。

657
00:31:00.700 --> 00:31:06.660
The guests are in suits and look great, seated on hay bales with white cloths covering the tops.
客人们穿着西装，看起来很棒，坐在铺着白布的干草垛上。

658
00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:12.440
Phyllis walks down the aisle with Angela riding on her back, smiling and nodding to all the guests.
菲利斯走在过道上，安吉拉骑在她背上，微笑着向所有客人点头。

659
00:31:12.740 --> 00:31:17.740
When she gets to the front, Angela daintily steps off and into the grave next to Dwight.
当她走到前面时，安吉拉优雅地走下来，进入德怀特旁边的坑里。

660
00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:24.880
But to make this walk down the aisle happen, well, first of all, Phyllis could not carry me down the aisle.
但为了实现这段走过道的情节，首先，菲利斯根本没法背着我走过道。

661
00:31:25.080 --> 00:31:26.620
That was not safe for her to do.
这对她来说不安全。

662
00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:35.140
So they actually got a stunt woman that had Phyllis' similar hair color that carried me down the aisle.
所以他们找了一位发色和菲利斯相似的替身演员背我走过道。

663
00:31:35.520 --> 00:31:37.100
And we had to practice this.
我们还得练习这个。

664
00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:37.980
I had a rehearsal.
我参加了排练。

665
00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:41.660
So we had to set up two different angles for the camera.
我们得为摄像机设置两个不同的角度。

666
00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:49.800
The camera that would be behind Phyllis and I walking down the aisle were really filming me on the back of the stunt woman.
拍我和菲利斯走过道背影的摄像机，其实拍的是我骑在替身演员背上。

667
00:31:49.940 --> 00:31:50.280
Okay.
好的。

668
00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:51.500
Because you couldn't see her face.
因为你看不见她的脸。

669
00:31:51.640 --> 00:31:52.980
And I am really being carried.
而且我确实是被背着的。

670
00:31:52.980 --> 00:31:55.100
And that's why you see my legs dangling.
这就是为什么你能看到我的腿在晃荡。

671
00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:55.840
Right?
对吧？

672
00:31:56.060 --> 00:31:56.320
Yes.
是的。

673
00:31:56.620 --> 00:32:00.620
But, of course, they also needed a shot of us coming towards the camera.
但当然，他们也需要拍我们迎面走来的镜头。

674
00:32:01.020 --> 00:32:13.020
And as we walked towards the camera, it was actually Phyllis and me behind her on this wooden plank being held by two men.
当我们朝摄像机走来时，其实是菲利斯和我，我站在两个男人抬着的木板上。

675
00:32:13.700 --> 00:32:14.200
Yes.
是的。

676
00:32:14.420 --> 00:32:18.720
And we had to practice the walk together because Phyllis does one step together.
我们必须一起练习走路，因为菲利斯走的是那种并步走。

677
00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:23.880
You know that traditional kind of walk down the aisle where you take one step and then your feet come together and you take one step.
你知道那种传统的走过道方式，迈一步，双脚并拢，再迈一步。

678
00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.400
So we had to practice this.
所以我们得练习这个。

679
00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:34.500
And there was one time where Phyllis got too far ahead and my arms are on her neck and the men with the plank did not meet her and I almost fell off the thing.
有一次菲利斯走得太快了，我的手还搂着她的脖子，抬木板的人没跟上，我差点从上面掉下来。

680
00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:36.440
It was such a crazy thing.
那真是太疯狂了。

681
00:32:36.440 --> 00:32:40.220
It was such a crazy thing to see, Angela, because we're all sitting there being the wedding guests.
安吉拉，看到那一幕真的很疯狂，因为我们当时都坐在那儿当婚礼嘉宾。

682
00:32:40.220 --> 00:32:48.280
And, you know, the two guys holding you on a piece of wood and you're sort of holding on to Phyllis.
你知道，两个男人抬着你站在一块木板上，你还得抓着菲利斯。

683
00:32:48.420 --> 00:32:51.940
And then they removed the guys in poSt.
然后他们在后期把那几个人去掉了。

684
00:32:52.160 --> 00:32:52.880
And the wood.
还有那块木板。

685
00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:59.100
Which is so crazy to me because I remember I turned to John and I was like, I don't understand.
这让我觉得太疯狂了，我记得我转头对约翰说，我不明白。

686
00:32:59.740 --> 00:33:01.340
We can just paint them out.
我们可以直接把他们涂掉。

687
00:33:01.520 --> 00:33:03.340
We can just get rid of them.
我们可以把他们处理掉。

688
00:33:03.620 --> 00:33:03.820
Yeah.
是啊。

689
00:33:03.820 --> 00:33:04.860
He was like, uh-huh.
他说，嗯哼。

690
00:33:05.060 --> 00:33:05.460
They did.
他们确实做到了。

691
00:33:05.940 --> 00:33:08.040
There's a whole wooden plank in two men.
那儿本来有一整块木板和两个男人。

692
00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:14.440
You wouldn't expect that on The Office there would be like an elaborate special effects moment.
你不会想到《办公室》里竟然会有这种复杂的特效镜头。

693
00:33:14.900 --> 00:33:15.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

694
00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:16.380
But this was.
但确实有。

695
00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:21.160
This was of the caliber of something you might see in The Matrix, dare I say.
我敢说，这简直达到了《黑客帝国》那种水准。

696
00:33:21.460 --> 00:33:21.980
Exactly.
没错。

697
00:33:22.320 --> 00:33:24.380
Oh, thank you for bringing The Matrix into the finale.
哦，谢谢你把《黑客帝国》带进大结局里。

698
00:33:24.380 --> 00:33:28.280
I needed Keanu to be here with us in some way for the finale.
我需要基努以某种方式和我们一起出现在大结局里。

699
00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:29.480
I really appreciate that.
我真的很感激。

700
00:33:29.480 --> 00:33:34.780
There are so many things that have happened to us over the last five years since we have been making this podcaSt.
自从我们开始做这个播客以来的过去五年里，发生了太多事情。

701
00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:36.480
I was going over them in my head.
我刚才在脑子里把它们过了一遍。

702
00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:42.920
I was thinking of life and just world events and all kinds of things.
我在思考人生，思考世界大事，还有各种各样的事情。

703
00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:52.000
And I was filled with such gratitude for all the things that we've done, you know, over these five years.
我心中充满了感激，为了我们这五年里一起完成的所有事情，你知道的。

704
00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:55.580
But I thought, I am not done here, though.
但我心想，我还没结束呢。

705
00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:57.480
I am not done.
我还没结束。

706
00:33:57.480 --> 00:34:05.120
And the one thing, the one thing that we have not managed to capture in this five years is Keanu.
有一件事，只有这一件事，是我们这五年里还没能做到的，那就是基努。

707
00:34:05.820 --> 00:34:06.660
I know.
我知道。

708
00:34:06.860 --> 00:34:09.640
And so we cannot stop podcasting.
所以我们不能停止做播客。

709
00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:10.580
Until.
直到。

710
00:34:10.920 --> 00:34:12.400
Until we have that.
直到我们做到为止。

711
00:34:12.620 --> 00:34:14.460
Until we get to interview Keanu.
直到我们能采访到基努。

712
00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:18.780
You know, he's going to be on Broadway and waiting for Godot with Alex Winter.
你知道，他要和亚历克斯·温特一起去百老汇演《等待戈多》了。

713
00:34:20.400 --> 00:34:22.120
And that's next fall.
就在明年秋天。

714
00:34:22.180 --> 00:34:25.160
And I feel like that's a reason to come talk to us.
我觉得这是一个让他来和我们聊聊的好理由。

715
00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:27.820
Maybe we go to the play.
也许我们可以去看那场戏。

716
00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:30.560
And then we talk to him in New York City.
然后我们在纽约市采访他。

717
00:34:31.060 --> 00:34:35.680
Well, lady, you know, any reason to go to New York City and see a play, I'm all over it.
好吧，女士，你知道的，任何去纽约看戏的理由，我都举双手赞成。

718
00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:36.840
Done.
成交。

719
00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:37.520
Done.
成交。

720
00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:43.080
I do want to say, while we've been talking, our balloons that say congrats have fallen.
我想说，就在我们聊天的时候，我们那写着“恭喜”的气球掉下来了。

721
00:34:46.300 --> 00:34:48.640
They're hanging on by one string.
它们现在只剩一根绳子挂着了。

722
00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:51.300
We have a few other things to cover from this scene.
我们还有这一场戏里的其他几点要讲。

723
00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:58.300
Number one, I want to say I think Greg Daniels should have won an Emmy for this episode, in particular for all these wedding scenes.
第一，我想说，我觉得格雷格·丹尼尔斯应该凭这一集拿艾美奖，尤其是为了这些婚礼场景。

724
00:34:58.580 --> 00:35:00.300
They are so funny.
它们太搞笑了。

725
00:35:00.400 --> 00:35:00.960
So funny.
太搞笑了。

726
00:35:01.060 --> 00:35:01.920
And so well done.
而且拍得真好。

727
00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:10.820
Again, I love that even though Angela Martin is on Phyllis's back, she is still waving to people who are seated.
再说一次，我喜欢这一点：尽管安吉拉·马丁正趴在菲利斯背上，她还在向坐着的人挥手。

728
00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:13.840
Kind of awkwardly, my hand is in Phyllis's face.
姿势有点尴尬，我的手就在菲利斯的脸上。

729
00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:17.620
I'm holding a bouquet in the other hand while I'm trying to hold on.
我另一只手还拿着花束，同时还得努力抓稳。

730
00:35:18.300 --> 00:35:22.500
I love that Kevin fist bumps Angela and she fist bumps him back.
我喜欢凯文和安吉拉碰拳，而她也回敬了他。

731
00:35:22.660 --> 00:35:25.480
And Meredith gives her real enthusiastic thumbs up.
还有梅雷迪思给了她一个非常热情的点赞。

732
00:35:25.720 --> 00:35:27.160
Those were improv moments.
那些都是即兴发挥的时刻。

733
00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:29.840
And it's just such a happy thing.
那真是一件让人开心的事。

734
00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:33.800
And then when Angela crawls into her, Michael comes over and gives her a hug.
然后当安吉拉爬到她身上时，迈克尔走过来给了她一个拥抱。

735
00:35:33.920 --> 00:35:34.980
That was not in the script.
那不在剧本里。

736
00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:36.760
Steve did that in the moment.
那是史蒂夫当时即兴做的。

737
00:35:37.340 --> 00:35:38.880
And I love it.
我太喜欢了。

738
00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.700
I'm just so happy to see him.
见到他我真是太高兴了。

739
00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:42.040
I'm hugging him for real.
我是真的在拥抱他。

740
00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:44.300
31 minutes, 6 seconds.
31分06秒。

741
00:35:44.440 --> 00:35:47.700
I want to give a shout out to the couple who I assume are playing Angela's parents.
我想向那对夫妇致意，我猜他们演的是安吉拉的父母。

742
00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:51.040
They're in the front row, both tiny folks, both blonde.
他们坐在前排，都是小个子，都是金发。

743
00:35:51.040 --> 00:36:00.140
And then when Oscar comes down the aisle with Philip, the woman playing Angela's mother is just gazing at Philip like a grandma would.
然后当奥斯卡抱着菲利普走过过道时，演安吉拉母亲的那个女人正像祖母一样凝视着菲利普。

744
00:36:00.820 --> 00:36:04.100
I also want to give a shout out to Michael Tuba Hethernton.
我还想向迈克尔·图巴·赫瑟顿致意。

745
00:36:04.220 --> 00:36:05.180
He is back.
他又回来了。

746
00:36:05.180 --> 00:36:06.300
He is the minister.
他就是那个牧师。

747
00:36:07.160 --> 00:36:09.080
And he's going to marry Dwight and Angela.
他要为德怀特和安吉拉主持婚礼。

748
00:36:09.560 --> 00:36:12.540
Yes, that's Veda's husband, Veda, our script supervisor.
没错，那是维达的丈夫，维达是我们剧组的剧本主管。

749
00:36:12.540 --> 00:36:14.600
And he was the minister in the farm.
他之前在农场那集里也是演牧师。

750
00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.260
But he's had multiple roles on the show.
但他在这部剧里演过好几个角色。

751
00:36:17.460 --> 00:36:18.380
Yes, we've broken him down.
没错，我们已经把他彻底击垮了。

752
00:36:18.540 --> 00:36:20.020
He has been so many different characters.
他演过太多不同的角色了。

753
00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:24.360
He's sort of like our soap star who keeps coming back as different characters.
他就像我们的肥皂剧明星，总是以不同的角色回归。

754
00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:25.080
He is.
确实如此。

755
00:36:25.080 --> 00:36:27.280
Or like Kirk from Gilmore Girls.
或者就像《吉尔莫女孩》里的柯克。

756
00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:35.400
You know, Sean Gunn played the character of Kirk on Gilmore Girls, but he has like multiple jobs and like even for a while had multiple names.
你知道，肖恩·古恩在《吉尔莫女孩》里饰演柯克这个角色，但他有好几份工作，甚至有一段时间还有好几个名字。

757
00:36:35.660 --> 00:36:37.540
Oh, very much like Kirk then.
哦，那确实很像柯克。

758
00:36:37.680 --> 00:36:37.920
Yes.
是的。

759
00:36:38.060 --> 00:36:41.740
