我得说，我相信他们当时都是单身。

883
00:41:19.450 --> 00:41:19.610
So.
所以。

884
00:41:19.810 --> 00:41:21.150
Single and in the bushes.
单身，还在灌木丛里。

885
00:41:24.990 --> 00:41:25.390
Okay.
好吧。

886
00:41:25.390 --> 00:41:26.170
Where are we?
我们说到哪了？

887
00:41:26.490 --> 00:41:26.890
Okay.
好吧。

888
00:41:26.890 --> 00:41:31.730
I know one thing I want to talk about, which is now the minister pronounces them man and
我知道有一件事我想聊聊，就是牧师宣布他们结为夫妻之后，

889
00:41:31.730 --> 00:41:34.090
wife, and he says, release the doves.
他说，放飞鸽子。

890
00:41:34.410 --> 00:41:34.710
Yeah.
是啊。

891
00:41:34.990 --> 00:41:36.170
The doves do not move.
鸽子没动。

892
00:41:36.370 --> 00:41:36.830
They do not.
它们确实没动。

893
00:41:37.010 --> 00:41:40.170
Everyone has this huge reaction, like, what?
每个人都有巨大的反应，就像，啊？

894
00:41:40.470 --> 00:41:44.750
Like, the reaction does not match what's happening, in my opinion.
在我看来，那种反应和正在发生的事情完全不匹配。

895
00:41:45.110 --> 00:41:46.710
Like, so the doves don't fly away.
就像是，鸽子没飞走而已。

896
00:41:46.830 --> 00:41:47.910
People wouldn't be like, what?
人们不至于那样，啊？

897
00:41:48.310 --> 00:41:49.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

898
00:41:49.270 --> 00:41:52.550
Does it feel like bad luck that the doves don't fly?
鸽子不飞走感觉像是坏兆头吗？

899
00:41:52.790 --> 00:41:53.110
Well.
嗯。

900
00:41:53.110 --> 00:41:56.250
That was how I interpreted it, that everybody was like, oh, no.
我是这么解读的，大家都觉得，噢，不。

901
00:41:56.250 --> 00:41:58.490
Oh, the doves aren't flying for their love.
哦，鸽子不是为了它们的爱情而飞的。

902
00:41:59.230 --> 00:42:00.370
For their love.
为了它们的爱情。

903
00:42:01.290 --> 00:42:02.770
So funny how you said that.
你刚才那么说真有意思。

904
00:42:03.550 --> 00:42:06.190
Well, I'll tell you, there was a reason.
嗯，我告诉你，这是有原因的。

905
00:42:06.910 --> 00:42:07.150
Okay.
好吧。

906
00:42:07.590 --> 00:42:09.630
So I remember this gag for the wedding.
我记得婚礼上有这么个桥段。

907
00:42:09.890 --> 00:42:11.890
I remember talking about it with Phil.
我记得和菲尔讨论过这件事。

908
00:42:12.190 --> 00:42:16.290
The idea was that one of the things Angela had on her registry were cats.
当时的想法是，安吉拉在她的结婚登记清单里列了一项：猫。

909
00:42:16.490 --> 00:42:17.790
She could bring her cats.
她可以带上她的猫。

910
00:42:18.010 --> 00:42:19.810
They have this basket of cats.
他们有一个装猫的篮子。

911
00:42:20.230 --> 00:42:25.830
Well, it said in the shooting draft, after the minister says, release the doves,
剧本初稿里写着，在牧师说“放飞鸽子”之后，

912
00:42:25.830 --> 00:42:30.830
Nate bends to the wicker cage that has a dozen cats clawing at it.
内特弯腰去打开那个有十几只猫在里面抓挠的柳条笼子。

913
00:42:31.050 --> 00:42:33.750
He shoos the cats away and opens a door.
他把猫赶走，然后打开门。

914
00:42:34.250 --> 00:42:37.230
Doves shoot out in a hurry to get the hell out of there.
鸽子急匆匆地飞出来，想赶紧逃离那个鬼地方。

915
00:42:37.810 --> 00:42:38.770
Everyone applauds.
大家都鼓掌。

916
00:42:39.070 --> 00:42:39.370
Okay.
好吧。

917
00:42:39.910 --> 00:42:45.070
