所以就是这样。

1386
01:02:56.850 --> 01:03:00.870
When Jim and Pam arrive home, Pam does not have a flower in her hair.
当吉姆和帕姆回到家时，帕姆头发上已经没有花了。

1387
01:03:01.390 --> 01:03:03.110
And they are tired.
而且他们很累。

1388
01:03:03.330 --> 01:03:04.830
Pam's like, oh, this day.
帕姆说，噢，这一天。

1389
01:03:05.050 --> 01:03:09.530
I mean, yeah, because you still have to go change clothes and go to another event.
我是说，确实，因为你还得换衣服去参加另一个活动。

1390
01:03:10.110 --> 01:03:11.730
But guess who walks out of their house?
但你猜谁从他们房子里走出来了？

1391
01:03:11.870 --> 01:03:12.510
Nancy Correll.
南希·科雷尔。

1392
01:03:12.510 --> 01:03:15.890
Nancy Correll, because Pam has sold their house.
南希·科雷尔，因为帕姆把他们的房子卖了。

1393
01:03:16.210 --> 01:03:19.270
I have so many bulls**t cards to play here.
我手里有太多胡扯的牌可以打了。

1394
01:03:19.270 --> 01:03:20.630
Well, yes.
嗯，确实。

1395
01:03:21.170 --> 01:03:24.930
There's this really fun scene where Jim's like, what's happening?
有个特别有趣的场景，吉姆问，发生什么事了？

1396
01:03:25.070 --> 01:03:25.750
Who are these people?
这些人是谁？

1397
01:03:26.330 --> 01:03:29.670
Carol walks out of their house with a couple of potential homebuyers.
卡罗尔带着几个潜在的购房者从他们房子里走出来。

1398
01:03:30.190 --> 01:03:37.030
And this is when Pam says, I just wanted to say thank you for being so great this past year.
这时帕姆说，我只是想谢谢你过去这一年对我这么好。

1399
01:03:37.910 --> 01:03:41.130
And I don't want you to have to give up anything to be with me.
我不想让你为了和我在一起而放弃任何东西。

1400
01:03:41.290 --> 01:03:45.050
So to show you how much I love you and to show you how much I believe in your future,
所以为了向你证明我有多爱你，也为了证明我有多相信你的未来，

1401
01:03:45.510 --> 01:03:48.930
I have been showing our house for about two months.
我带人看我们的房子已经有两个月了。

1402
01:03:49.210 --> 01:03:49.710
Two months.
两个月。

1403
01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:50.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1404
01:03:50.310 --> 01:03:51.810
He's like, oh, that's why it's so clean.
他说，噢，难怪家里这么干净。

1405
01:03:51.970 --> 01:03:52.690
She's like, uh-huh.
她说，嗯哼。

1406
01:03:52.810 --> 01:03:53.070
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1407
01:03:53.710 --> 01:03:57.030
And then she has this line, you know, you bought it without telling me.
然后她说了句，你知道，你没跟我商量就把房子买了。

1408
01:03:57.150 --> 01:03:59.590
I thought maybe I could sell it without telling you.
我以为我也能不跟你商量就把房子卖了。

1409
01:04:00.490 --> 01:04:00.930
Kaboom.
砰。

1410
01:04:01.970 --> 01:04:03.530
This is such a great marriage.
这婚姻真是太棒了。

1411
01:04:04.490 --> 01:04:05.550
This is, okay.
这，好吧。

1412
01:04:05.870 --> 01:04:06.890
Thank you for saying that.
谢谢你这么说。

1413
01:04:07.070 --> 01:04:10.690
I know that this is supposed to be a big romantic gesture.
我知道这本该是一个重大的浪漫举动。

1414
01:04:10.690 --> 01:04:18.170
It feels a little tit for tat, but I know for the story, they want Pam and Jim to be able
感觉有点针锋相对，但我知道为了剧情需要，他们想让帕姆和吉姆能够

1415
01:04:18.170 --> 01:04:20.450
to move on together, you know?
一起继续生活，你懂吗？

1416
01:04:20.970 --> 01:04:21.230
Yes.
是的。

1417
01:04:21.670 --> 01:04:24.370
Jim got his big moment with the teapot.
吉姆已经有过那个茶壶的高光时刻了。

1418
01:04:24.730 --> 01:04:26.730
They wanted Pam to have a big moment.
他们想让帕姆也有一个高光时刻。

1419
01:04:27.110 --> 01:04:33.790
But I said in the writer's room, I said, I'm not sure that the answer to this couple's problems
但我在编剧室里说过，我说，我不确定这对情侣解决问题的办法

1420
01:04:33.790 --> 01:04:40.670
is for Pam to adopt this habit of making big life moves without consulting the other person.
就是让帕姆养成这种不跟对方商量就做出重大人生决定的习惯。

1421
01:04:40.930 --> 01:04:41.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1422
01:04:41.370 --> 01:04:43.430
They don't want to be the gotcha couple.
他们不想成为那种互相算计的情侣。

1423
01:04:43.910 --> 01:04:44.410
Gotcha.
抓到你了。

1424
01:04:44.670 --> 01:04:45.470
Sold the house.
房子卖了。

1425
01:04:45.730 --> 01:04:46.130
I know.
我知道。

1426
01:04:46.290 --> 01:04:47.830
It's like, here's what we're doing now.
就像是，这就是我们现在要做的。

1427
01:04:49.610 --> 01:04:54.330
Actually, originally, they were going to come home and there was going to be a sold sign
其实最初，他们本来打算回家时看到院子里

1428
01:04:54.330 --> 01:04:55.030
in the yard.
插着一块已售出的牌子。

1429
01:04:55.390 --> 01:04:57.230
And Jim was going to be like, what's this?
然后吉姆会问，这是怎么回事？

1430
01:04:57.930 --> 01:05:04.070
So I said, maybe their big romantic gesture is that she's been showing the house.
所以我说，也许他们重大的浪漫举动是她一直在带人看房。

1431
01:05:04.850 --> 01:05:11.050
But you notice in the scene, they do actually decide together to do the move.
但你注意到在那场戏里，他们确实是一起决定搬家的。

1432
01:05:11.150 --> 01:05:12.890
The people say, we'll take it.
买家说，我们要了。

1433
01:05:13.010 --> 01:05:14.750
And then Pam kind of looks at Jim.
然后帕姆看了看吉姆。

1434
01:05:14.930 --> 01:05:17.710
So in a way, Pam is like offering an opportunity.
所以在某种程度上，帕姆是在提供一个机会。

1435
01:05:18.930 --> 01:05:23.790
And then they do finally agree on something together in the moment.
然后他们最终在那一刻就某事达成了一致。

1436
01:05:23.950 --> 01:05:25.210
And I was like, okay, I like that.
我就觉得，好吧，我喜欢这样。

1437
01:05:25.350 --> 01:05:26.570
That does feel romantic.
那确实感觉很浪漫。

1438
01:05:26.950 --> 01:05:27.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
01:05:27.230 --> 01:05:28.270
And they hug.
然后他们拥抱了。

1440
01:05:28.470 --> 01:05:29.710
They're super happy.
他们超级开心。

1441
01:05:29.970 --> 01:05:34.110
I did love that both Steve and Nancy got to be in the finale.
我确实很高兴史蒂夫和南希都能出现在大结局里。

1442
01:05:34.390 --> 01:05:35.790
I thought that was really nice.
我觉得那真的很棒。

1443
01:05:36.050 --> 01:05:36.370
Yes.
是的。

1444
01:05:36.510 --> 01:05:41.070
And the home buyer was played by Jay Falk, our season nine script coordinator.
而那个购房者是由我们第九季的剧本协调员杰伊·福克饰演的。

1445
01:05:42.010 --> 01:05:45.750
Well, Pam and Jim are now going to arrive at the PBS viewing party.
好了，帕姆和吉姆现在要到达PBS的观看派对了。

1446
01:05:46.030 --> 01:05:48.870
It was described in the shooting draft like this.
拍摄剧本中是这样描述的。

1447
01:05:49.490 --> 01:05:50.610
Interior warehouse.
仓库内景。

1448
01:05:51.030 --> 01:05:54.190
We see people from the office mixing with various members of the crew.
我们看到办公室的人员与剧组的各个成员混在一起。

1449
01:05:54.190 --> 01:05:59.470
There is a promotional backdrop with the logo for the office and American workplace on it.
有一个印有《办公室》和《美国职场》标志的宣传背景板。

1450
01:05:59.470 --> 01:06:02.830
Kevin and Meredith pose with several executives for a picture.
凯文和梅雷迪思与几位高管合影留念。

1451
01:06:03.230 --> 01:06:05.450
After the picture is taken, they try to walk away.
拍完照后，他们试图走开。

1452
01:06:05.570 --> 01:06:08.550
But another group approaches them and they have to pose for another picture.
但另一群人走过来，他们不得不停下来再拍一张。

1453
01:06:08.550 --> 01:06:11.410
There is a table with food and refreshments.
桌上摆着食物和茶点。

1454
01:06:11.410 --> 01:06:15.910
And another table is full of office and American workplace swag.
另一张桌子上摆满了办公室用品和美式职场周边。

1455
01:06:16.770 --> 01:06:18.990
Phyllis and Stanley are examining the swag.
菲利斯和斯坦利正在查看那些周边。

1456
01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:26.290
Phyllis takes a mug and a production person stops her and says, these are for PBS executives only.
菲利斯拿了一个马克杯，一个工作人员拦住她说，这些是留给PBS高管的。

1457
01:06:26.290 --> 01:06:30.010
Well, the person who says that is Allison Jones.
那个说这话的人是艾莉森·琼斯。

1458
01:06:30.210 --> 01:06:30.710
That's right.
没错。

1459
01:06:30.990 --> 01:06:34.830
She said Greg really wanted her to be in a scene and she was kind of reluctant.
她说格雷格真的很想让她出镜，她当时还有点不情愿。

1460
01:06:34.830 --> 01:06:38.310
But she said, I'll do it if my scene is with Phyllis.
但她说，如果能和菲利斯演对手戏，我就答应。

1461
01:06:38.490 --> 01:06:38.830
Aw.
噢。

1462
01:06:39.210 --> 01:06:41.130
Because they were co-workers, you know?
因为她们是同事，你知道的。

1463
01:06:41.310 --> 01:06:41.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1464
01:06:42.410 --> 01:06:47.090
There is now a montage of scenes of everyone mixing and mingling and talking.
现在是一段蒙太奇剪辑，大家都在交际、寒暄和聊天。

1465
01:06:47.390 --> 01:06:47.590
Yeah.
没错。

1466
01:06:47.590 --> 01:06:54.510
Pam is going to unveil her big mural, her warehouse mural called The History of Us.
帕姆准备揭幕她的大型壁画，那幅名为《我们的历史》的仓库壁画。

1467
01:06:54.690 --> 01:07:02.090
She dedicates it to Jim and the crowd applauds and Pam says, oh, let's take a photo in front of it.
她把它献给吉姆，人群鼓掌，帕姆说，噢，我们在壁画前拍张照吧。

1468
01:07:02.210 --> 01:07:04.710
And all these people crowd in for the photo.
然后所有人都挤过来合影。

1469
01:07:05.070 --> 01:07:09.490
This was another opportunity for Greg to get some of our crew members in there.
这是格雷格让我们的剧组成员出镜的又一个机会。

1470
01:07:09.670 --> 01:07:10.350
And Greg.
还有格雷格。

1471
01:07:10.650 --> 01:07:11.070
And Greg.
还有格雷格。

1472
01:07:11.230 --> 01:07:13.070
Greg is who has his arm around Pam.
搂着帕姆肩膀的那个人就是格雷格。

1473
01:07:13.070 --> 01:07:19.610
I thought this was really moving to watch because you see so many faces from our show.
我觉得这一幕看得很感人，因为你能看到我们剧组的这么多面孔。

1474
01:07:19.810 --> 01:07:25.310
So many of our amazing crew, our writers, our producers, our editors, the directors, the caSt.
我们这么多出色的剧组成员、编剧、制片人、剪辑师、导演和演员。

1475
01:07:25.550 --> 01:07:33.550
And you get to hear Kate Flannery's real life boyfriend, Chris Haston's voice as he's taking the pictures.
你还能听到凯特·弗兰纳里的现实男友克里斯·哈斯顿在拍照时的声音。

1476
01:07:34.090 --> 01:07:34.270
Yes.
是的。

1477
01:07:34.270 --> 01:07:40.550
I noticed Howard Kline, Stephanie, R-A-D, who I recently texted about my party.
我注意到了霍华德·克莱恩、斯蒂芬妮、R-A-D，我最近还发短信跟她聊过我的派对。

1478
01:07:41.090 --> 01:07:43.970
Rusty Mahmood, Veda, Dave Rogers is in there.
拉斯蒂·马哈茂德、维达，戴夫·罗杰斯也在里面。

1479
01:07:44.110 --> 01:07:45.290
Claire Scanlon is in there.
克莱尔·斯坎伦也在里面。

1480
01:07:45.370 --> 01:07:46.850
There's so many people.
有好多人啊。

1481
01:07:47.070 --> 01:07:47.890
It's like.
就像是。

1482
01:07:48.610 --> 01:07:49.890
It's our show.
这就是我们的剧。

1483
01:07:50.090 --> 01:07:50.670
It's our show.
这就是我们的剧。

1484
01:07:50.810 --> 01:07:51.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1485
01:07:51.250 --> 01:07:52.110
It's our show family.
这是我们的剧组大家庭。

1486
01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:54.570
We had a question from Mary M.
我们收到一个来自马里兰州玛丽·M的问题。

1487
01:07:54.730 --> 01:07:57.490
from Maryland who said, who painted Pam's mural?
她问，帕姆的壁画是谁画的？

1488
01:07:58.730 --> 01:08:01.190
Well, Mary, it was painted by Jules Comesco.
嗯，玛丽，那是朱尔斯·科梅斯科画的。

1489
01:08:01.190 --> 01:08:03.450
She's the person who did all of our office art.
她负责了我们办公室所有的艺术创作。

1490
01:08:03.470 --> 01:08:04.770
But here's the thing.
但重点是。

1491
01:08:04.950 --> 01:08:08.350
It was not finished when we had to shoot this scene.
我们拍这场戏的时候，壁画还没画完。

1492
01:08:08.810 --> 01:08:11.050
It was still in the conception phase.
它还处于构思阶段。

1493
01:08:11.270 --> 01:08:15.170
Like Greg was still making tweaks to what this mural would be.
格雷格当时还在对壁画的内容做调整。

1494
01:08:15.970 --> 01:08:19.710
So we are actually posing and reacting in front of a blank wall.
所以我们实际上是在对着一面空白的墙摆姿势和做出反应。

1495
01:08:20.390 --> 01:08:25.990
Steve Burgess said that they were working on this mural until the very last minute, until 2 a.m.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，他们为了这幅壁画一直忙到最后一刻，直到凌晨两点。

1496
01:08:26.110 --> 01:08:27.810
the night before the episode aired.
就在剧集播出前一天晚上。

1497
01:08:28.030 --> 01:08:28.750
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1498
01:08:28.750 --> 01:08:31.110
She never painted it on the wall.
她从来没在墙上画过。

1499
01:08:31.310 --> 01:08:37.170
She painted a smaller version, which they then superimposed onto the wall in poSt.
她画了一个较小的版本，然后后期制作时叠加到了墙上。

1500
01:08:37.370 --> 01:08:40.910
And that smaller version he thinks Greg got to keep.
而那个较小的版本，他觉得被格雷格留下了。

1501
01:08:41.170 --> 01:08:42.690
Oh, that's really cool.
噢，那真的很酷。

1502
01:08:42.890 --> 01:08:43.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1503
01:08:43.830 --> 01:08:49.950
Well, in this montage of the PBS party, we also do see Dave Rogers and Terry Weinberg.
嗯，在PBS派对的这段剪辑里，我们还看到了戴夫·罗杰斯和特里·温伯格。

1504
01:08:50.130 --> 01:08:54.150
They even have a little scene together, and it's in deleted scenes.
他们甚至还有一段对手戏，不过是在删减片段里。

1505
01:08:54.430 --> 01:09:02.170
Well, now you see the employees giving each other little sly glances and sort of motioning toward the staircase that goes nowhere.
嗯，现在你可以看到员工们互相使眼色，还示意对方看向那条通往死胡同的楼梯。

1506
01:09:03.010 --> 01:09:09.190
And that's because they have plans to have their own little Dunder Mifflin party up in the bullpen.
那是因为他们打算在办公区举办他们自己的邓德·米夫林小派对。

1507
01:09:09.370 --> 01:09:09.610
Yep.
没错。

1508
01:09:10.130 --> 01:09:14.430
And when they get up there, the phone rings just as Jim and Pam are entering.
当他们上去的时候，电话正好在吉姆和帕姆进来时响了。

1509
01:09:14.730 --> 01:09:17.990
Jim goes and sits at his desk, and Pam notices the phone is ringing.
吉姆走过去坐在办公桌前，帕姆注意到电话在响。

1510
01:09:17.990 --> 01:09:20.330
And she answers it.
于是她接起了电话。

1511
01:09:20.510 --> 01:09:22.670
She says, Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.
她说：“邓德·米夫林，我是帕姆。”

1512
01:09:22.670 --> 01:09:31.070
I really wanted to say that line one more time because I improvised that in one of our early morning work sessions on the pilot.
我真的很想再说一次这句台词，因为这是我在拍摄试播集时，某次清晨工作会议上即兴发挥的。

1513
01:09:32.650 --> 01:09:36.210
And I remember Greg saying, oh, that's so good.
我记得格雷格当时说，噢，那太棒了。

1514
01:09:36.290 --> 01:09:37.110
That's so realistic.
那太真实了。

1515
01:09:37.610 --> 01:09:40.270
And I said, well, that's how I used to answer the phone at all my jobs.
我说，嗯，我以前在所有工作岗位上都是这么接电话的。

1516
01:09:40.270 --> 01:09:41.970
I would say the company, this is Jenna.
我会说“某某公司，我是珍娜”。

1517
01:09:42.250 --> 01:09:42.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1518
01:09:42.890 --> 01:09:44.110
And he goes, I love that.
他说，我喜欢这个。

1519
01:09:44.230 --> 01:09:45.210
That's a great detail.
这是一个很棒的细节。

1520
01:09:45.550 --> 01:09:48.550
And that then became part of my character.
后来这就成了我角色的一部分。

1521
01:09:48.950 --> 01:09:49.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1522
01:09:49.410 --> 01:09:51.570
So that was one of the things I said to Greg.
所以那是我对格雷格提出的要求之一。

1523
01:09:51.570 --> 01:09:54.070
I had very interesting requests for the finale.
我对大结局有一些非常有趣的要求。

1524
01:09:54.330 --> 01:10:00.090
I was like, I want a scene with all the ladies, and I want one more chance of saying, Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.
我说，我想要一场所有女士都在场的戏，我还想再有机会说一次“邓德·米夫林，我是帕姆”。

1525
01:10:00.290 --> 01:10:07.450
Because I haven't been the receptionist for a long time, and I wanted to sit behind that desk just one more time before the show was over.
因为我已经很久没当接待员了，在剧集结束前，我想再坐在那张桌子后面一次。

1526
01:10:07.770 --> 01:10:08.970
Well, I loved it.
嗯，我喜欢这个安排。

1527
01:10:09.150 --> 01:10:10.410
I mean, Jim clocks it.
我是说，吉姆注意到了。

1528
01:10:10.490 --> 01:10:11.650
He immediately looks up.
他立刻抬起头来。

1529
01:10:11.730 --> 01:10:14.530
It probably took him back in time to their early days.
这大概让他回想起了他们刚开始的日子。

1530
01:10:14.970 --> 01:10:16.590
And Pam says, oh, I'm sorry.
然后帕姆说，噢，抱歉。

1531
01:10:16.850 --> 01:10:18.390
Jim Halpert doesn't work here anymore.
吉姆·哈珀特不在这里工作了。

1532
01:10:18.650 --> 01:10:18.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1533
01:10:18.910 --> 01:10:21.450
And then Pam has a talking head.
接着是帕姆的采访片段。

1534
01:10:21.650 --> 01:10:26.730
And, you know, I want to play it because I love it so much, Jenna.
而且，你知道吗，我想放出来听听，因为我太喜欢这段了，珍娜。

1535
01:10:26.890 --> 01:10:29.770
This is one of my favorite Pam talking heads of the whole series.
这是我整部剧里最喜欢的帕姆采访片段之一。

1536
01:10:29.950 --> 01:10:35.510
And I know a lot of people quote Pam's end final talking head.
我知道很多人都会引用帕姆最后那个采访片段。

1537
01:10:35.590 --> 01:10:35.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1538
01:10:35.890 --> 01:10:36.090
Right?
对吧？

1539
01:10:36.630 --> 01:10:39.630
That's a very famous one that gets quoted all the time.
那是很有名的一段，经常被人引用。

1540
01:10:39.790 --> 01:10:42.150
But this one is actually my favorite.
但这一段其实才是我的最爱。

1541
01:10:42.570 --> 01:10:43.410
Let's hear it.
我们来听听吧。

1542
01:10:43.410 --> 01:10:45.530
I didn't watch the whole documentary.
我没有看完整个纪录片。

1543
01:10:45.950 --> 01:10:48.030
After a few episodes, it was too painful.
看了几集之后，觉得太痛苦了。

1544
01:10:48.390 --> 01:10:50.410
I kept wanting to scream at Pam.
我一直想对着帕姆尖叫。

1545
01:10:51.170 --> 01:10:54.570
It took me so long to do so many important things.
我花了那么久才做成那么多重要的事情。

1546
01:10:54.570 --> 01:10:59.230
It's just hard to accept that I spent so many years being less happy than I could have been.
很难接受我竟然花了那么多年，过得比本可以拥有的生活更不快乐。

1547
01:11:00.410 --> 01:11:04.770
Jim was five feet from my desk, and it took me four years to get to him.
吉姆离我的办公桌只有五英尺远，但我花了四年才走到他身边。

1548
01:11:04.770 --> 01:11:09.350
It would be great if people saw this documentary and learned from my mistakes.
如果人们看了这部纪录片并能从我的错误中吸取教训，那就太好了。

1549
01:11:09.950 --> 01:11:11.490
Not that I'm a tragic person.
并不是说我是一个悲剧人物。

1550
01:11:11.490 --> 01:11:12.850
I'm really happy now.
我现在真的很快乐。

1551
01:11:13.290 --> 01:11:22.470
But it would just make my heart sore if someone out there saw this and she said to herself,
但如果有人看到这段话，并对自己说：

1552
01:11:23.150 --> 01:11:28.330
be strong, trust yourself, love yourself, conquer your fears.
要坚强，要相信自己，爱自己，战胜内心的恐惧。

1553
01:11:28.910 --> 01:11:34.490
Just go after what you want and act fast because life just isn't that long.
去追求你想要的，并且要快，因为人生苦短。

1554
01:11:36.010 --> 01:11:37.230
Isn't that beautiful?
这不是很美吗？

1555
01:11:37.630 --> 01:11:38.590
It's beautiful writing.
这段文字写得真美。

1556
01:11:38.870 --> 01:11:40.030
It's so beautiful.
太美了。

1557
01:11:40.290 --> 01:11:41.930
It's just so great.
真是太棒了。

1558
01:11:42.350 --> 01:11:42.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1559
01:11:43.450 --> 01:11:47.590
Well, it's beautiful writing, and your performance was just so great.
确实写得美，而且你的演绎也太棒了。

1560
01:11:47.770 --> 01:11:52.350
And, you know, this talking head, I think it just hit me differently than the first time I heard it.
而且，你知道吗，这段采访，我觉得它给我的触动和第一次听时完全不同。

1561
01:11:52.350 --> 01:11:59.650
I was in my 30s, and I haven't really, really listened to it in years.
那时候我才30多岁，之后真的好多年没再仔细听过了。

1562
01:11:59.650 --> 01:12:02.050
And now it just hits different at 53.
现在到了53岁，感觉完全不一样了。

1563
01:12:02.450 --> 01:12:03.250
It does.
确实如此。

1564
01:12:03.850 --> 01:12:04.970
It sure does.
确实是这样。

1565
01:12:05.610 --> 01:12:11.390
It's the wisdom of someone who's had a lot of life go by.
这是历经沧桑后才有的智慧。

1566
01:12:11.630 --> 01:12:11.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1567
01:12:12.670 --> 01:12:15.570
Be strong, trust yourself, love yourself.
要坚强，要相信自己，爱自己。

1568
01:12:15.890 --> 01:12:16.810
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1569
01:12:16.950 --> 01:12:17.610
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1570
01:12:17.810 --> 01:12:19.970
Well, in the background of that talking head,
在那段采访的背景里，

1571
01:12:19.970 --> 01:12:22.810
you saw a lot of moments from Jim and Pam's relationship.
你看到了吉姆和帕姆感情中的许多瞬间。

1572
01:12:22.810 --> 01:12:27.170
You saw this one yo-yo moment with Jim kind of.
你看到了吉姆玩悠悠球的那个片段。

1573
01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:30.370
That was us messing around on set.
那是我们在片场闹着玩。

1574
01:12:30.530 --> 01:12:32.090
That was not in an episode.
那不是剧集里的内容。

1575
01:12:32.630 --> 01:12:34.010
They just captured it.
他们只是把它拍了下来。

1576
01:12:34.010 --> 01:12:35.130
They just captured it.
他们只是把它拍了下来。

1577
01:12:35.210 --> 01:12:37.470
That was one of the many times that, like,
那是很多次这种情况之一，就像，

1578
01:12:38.530 --> 01:12:41.770
they would be rolling on us early, early on,
在很早的时候，他们就会提前开机拍摄我们，

1579
01:12:41.770 --> 01:12:46.230
and they just wanted us to do stuff to capture as B-roll.
他们只是想让我们做些什么来作为空镜素材。

1580
01:12:46.510 --> 01:12:50.690
And that was just one of the little things we came up with that Jim and Pam did.
那只是我们想出来的小花招之一，吉姆和帕姆会做的那种。

1581
01:12:50.690 --> 01:12:51.890
It was really cute.
真的很可爱。

1582
01:12:52.150 --> 01:12:52.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1583
01:12:52.570 --> 01:12:53.330
I loved seeing it.
我很高兴看到它。

1584
01:12:53.490 --> 01:12:54.650
It reminded me of those times.
它让我想起了那些时光。

1585
01:12:54.930 --> 01:12:57.050
I love seeing the passage of time.
我喜欢看到时光流逝的感觉。

1586
01:12:57.310 --> 01:13:00.830
It really showed you how long you got to know these characters
它真实地展现了你了解这些角色有多久，

1587
01:13:00.830 --> 01:13:03.510
and how long we played these characters.
以及我们扮演这些角色有多久。

1588
01:13:04.250 --> 01:13:04.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1589
01:13:04.730 --> 01:13:07.270
Well, the next talking head is Kevin.
好了，下一段采访是凯文的。

1590
01:13:07.590 --> 01:13:08.370
He says,
他说，

1591
01:13:08.530 --> 01:13:10.490
if there's one thing I've learned through this whole experience,
如果说我从整个经历中学到了什么，

1592
01:13:10.510 --> 01:13:12.370
it's that if you film anybody long enough,
那就是如果你拍摄一个人足够久，

1593
01:13:12.450 --> 01:13:13.590
they're going to do something stupid.
他们总会做出一些蠢事。

1594
01:13:13.590 --> 01:13:15.050
It's only human natural.
这是人之常情。

1595
01:13:15.350 --> 01:13:16.050
That's right.
没错。

1596
01:13:17.370 --> 01:13:19.630
And then Angela and Dwight come in.
然后安吉拉和德怀特进来了。

1597
01:13:19.950 --> 01:13:20.470
Yes.
是的。

1598
01:13:20.730 --> 01:13:22.610
Their honeymoon can wait, they say.
他们说，蜜月可以等等再说。

1599
01:13:23.310 --> 01:13:25.810
I'm so curious what their honeymoon was.
我真好奇他们的蜜月会是什么样。

1600
01:13:26.450 --> 01:13:26.970
Same.
我也是。

1601
01:13:27.870 --> 01:13:30.270
I do want to play a clip from this scene.
我想播放这一幕中的一个片段。

1602
01:13:30.510 --> 01:13:31.410
I've titled it,
我给它起名叫，

1603
01:13:31.570 --> 01:13:33.930
Guess Which Line I Had to ADr.
猜猜我哪句台词不得不后期配音。

1604
01:13:34.730 --> 01:13:35.110
Oh.
哦。

1605
01:13:35.290 --> 01:13:35.690
Okay.
好吧。

1606
01:13:35.870 --> 01:13:36.570
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1607
01:13:37.190 --> 01:13:37.790
Hey, guys.
嘿，伙计们。

1608
01:13:38.030 --> 01:13:38.370
Hi.
嗨。

1609
01:13:38.690 --> 01:13:38.790
Hey.
嘿。

1610
01:13:41.650 --> 01:13:42.750
What about the honeymoon?
那蜜月怎么办？

1611
01:13:43.130 --> 01:13:44.670
Oh, the honeymoon can wait till tomorrow.
哦，蜜月可以等到明天。

1612
01:13:45.010 --> 01:13:46.450
We wanted to hang out with you guys.
我们想和你们待在一起。

1613
01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:49.770
I mean, when are we all going to be here together again?
我是说，我们什么时候才能再像这样聚在一起呢？

1614
01:13:51.410 --> 01:13:52.350
Is that the line?
是那句台词吗？

1615
01:13:52.510 --> 01:13:54.530
When are we all going to be here together again?
我们什么时候才能再像这样聚在一起呢？

1616
01:13:54.750 --> 01:13:55.150
Yes.
是的。

1617
01:13:55.890 --> 01:13:57.370
Lady, that is so crazy.
天哪，那太疯狂了。

1618
01:13:57.570 --> 01:13:59.850
I did not know that you had to ADR that line.
我不知道你那句台词还得后期配音。

1619
01:13:59.990 --> 01:14:02.170
But when I was watching this episode,
但当我看这一集的时候，

1620
01:14:02.410 --> 01:14:03.290
I thought to myself,
我心想，

1621
01:14:03.290 --> 01:14:06.470
I don't remember Angela ever getting through that line.
我不记得安吉拉说过那句台词。

1622
01:14:06.750 --> 01:14:07.770
You kept crying.
你一直在哭。

1623
01:14:07.830 --> 01:14:10.090
Every time you said it, it got like stuck in your throat.
每次你说那句话，就像卡在喉咙里一样。

1624
01:14:10.370 --> 01:14:12.250
You couldn't get that line out.
你没法把那句台词说出来。

1625
01:14:12.370 --> 01:14:13.390
I couldn't get the line.
我确实说不出来。

1626
01:14:13.830 --> 01:14:15.170
I was too emotional.
我当时太激动了。

1627
01:14:15.170 --> 01:14:18.110
And then I had to go back and do it in ADr.
所以我不得不回去做后期配音。

1628
01:14:18.110 --> 01:14:23.970
So I actually got to see a little bit of the finale before it aired.
所以我其实在结局播出前就提前看到了那一小部分。

1629
01:14:24.810 --> 01:14:26.750
Just that scene, you know?
就那一幕，你知道吗？

1630
01:14:27.130 --> 01:14:33.590
And it was so wild to me because when I went to do the ADR, we had wrapped.
这对我来说太不可思议了，因为我去配音的时候，我们已经杀青了。

1631
01:14:33.810 --> 01:14:35.630
We had packed up our trailers.
我们已经收拾好拖车了。

1632
01:14:35.770 --> 01:14:39.110
We had taken everything we wanted to take from the set.
我们已经从片场拿走了所有想带走的东西。

1633
01:14:39.350 --> 01:14:40.190
We were gone.
我们已经离开了。

1634
01:14:40.630 --> 01:14:41.890
It was done.
一切都结束了。

1635
01:14:42.810 --> 01:14:45.810
And then they called me to do ADR at Universal.
然后他们叫我去环球影城做后期配音。

1636
01:14:46.770 --> 01:14:53.250
And for me, that was actually my last day of work on the office, was in this ADR booth.
对我来说，那才是我在《办公室》工作的最后一天，就在那个配音间里。

1637
01:14:53.890 --> 01:14:56.090
Saying that line that you couldn't get out.
说着那句你当时说不出来的台词。

1638
01:14:56.230 --> 01:14:57.190
That I couldn't get out.
我当时说不出来的台词。

1639
01:14:57.190 --> 01:15:02.930
And I have a picture of me in the booth because it says the office, you know?
我有一张在配音间里的照片，上面写着《办公室》，你知道吗？

1640
01:15:03.530 --> 01:15:05.710
And that was my last day of work.
那是我工作的最后一天。

1641
01:15:06.750 --> 01:15:13.550
Well, Dwight is going to propose a conference room meeting with Jim and Pam just for fun when he gets back from his honeymoon.
好吧，德怀特从蜜月回来后，本来打算为了好玩而提议和吉姆、帕姆开个会议室会议。

1642
01:15:14.290 --> 01:15:17.590
But Jim says, actually, we need to talk.
但吉姆说，其实，我们需要谈谈。

1643
01:15:18.550 --> 01:15:18.770
Yeah.
是的。

1644
01:15:19.730 --> 01:15:26.670
Pam and Jim go into Dwight's office and they share with him that they're going to follow Athleap to Austin.
帕姆和吉姆走进德怀特的办公室，告诉他他们要跟随Athleap去奥斯汀。

1645
01:15:26.930 --> 01:15:27.710
Austin now.
现在是奥斯汀了。

1646
01:15:27.970 --> 01:15:28.190
Yeah.
是的。

1647
01:15:28.650 --> 01:15:30.450
And Dwight says, no, don't say it.
德怀特说，不，别说出来。

1648
01:15:30.530 --> 01:15:31.010
You're fired.
你们被解雇了。

1649
01:15:31.170 --> 01:15:31.930
You're both fired.
你们两个都被解雇了。

1650
01:15:32.130 --> 01:15:33.490
And Jim's like, Dwight, come on.
吉姆说，德怀特，别这样。

1651
01:15:33.810 --> 01:15:35.250
Don't end on a bad note.
别以不愉快的方式收场。

1652
01:15:35.710 --> 01:15:39.350
But Dwight was saying that because now he can give them a severance package.
但德怀特那么说是因为他现在能给他们遣散费了。

1653
01:15:39.830 --> 01:15:40.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1654
01:15:40.170 --> 01:15:42.930
He says, in true Dwight fashion, don't be an idiot.
他说，用德怀特一贯的风格来说，别犯傻。

1655
01:15:43.810 --> 01:15:45.090
It's for the severance.
这是为了遣散费。

1656
01:15:45.250 --> 01:15:45.730
I know.
我知道。

1657
01:15:45.730 --> 01:15:50.210
And he gives them one month for every year they've been at Dunder Mifflin.
他给他们每在邓德·米夫林工作一年就发一个月工资作为遣散费。

1658
01:15:50.670 --> 01:15:52.390
So that's pretty nice.
所以这还挺不错的。

1659
01:15:52.430 --> 01:15:54.370
How long do we think they've been there?
你觉得他们在那儿待了多久了？

1660
01:15:54.450 --> 01:15:55.710
Like seven or eight years?
大概七八年？

1661
01:15:55.870 --> 01:15:58.330
Are they going to get like almost a year's severance pay?
他们能拿到差不多一年的遣散费吗？

1662
01:15:58.330 --> 01:15:59.070
That's what I thought.
我也是这么想的。

1663
01:15:59.190 --> 01:16:00.890
They're almost getting like a year's salary.
他们差不多能拿到一年的薪水。

1664
01:16:01.170 --> 01:16:01.910
That's a lot.
那可是一大笔钱。

1665
01:16:02.070 --> 01:16:02.810
Both of them.
他们两个都是。

1666
01:16:03.070 --> 01:16:03.810
Both of them.
他们两个都是。

1667
01:16:03.890 --> 01:16:04.290
Exactly.
没错。

1668
01:16:04.570 --> 01:16:04.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1669
01:16:04.790 --> 01:16:04.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1670
01:16:05.610 --> 01:16:07.150
Jim also says, and you know what?
吉姆还说，你知道吗？

1671
01:16:07.210 --> 01:16:10.590
If you're ever in Austin, and Dwight says, for what?
如果你哪天去奥斯汀，德怀特问，去干嘛？

1672
01:16:10.590 --> 01:16:13.070
The art, the music, the incredible nightlife?
为了艺术、音乐，还是精彩的夜生活？

1673
01:16:13.210 --> 01:16:14.070
No, thank you.
不，谢谢。

1674
01:16:14.290 --> 01:16:15.470
He's not interested.
他没兴趣。

1675
01:16:15.790 --> 01:16:18.810
But if you're ever in the area, you'll always have a place to stay.
但如果你哪天在那附近，随时都有地方住。

1676
01:16:19.390 --> 01:16:20.410
In my barn.
在我的谷仓里。

1677
01:16:20.870 --> 01:16:21.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1678
01:16:21.710 --> 01:16:22.910
Jim says, there it is.
吉姆说，这就对了。

1679
01:16:23.610 --> 01:16:28.170
And then we have a Dwight talking head that I just really, really love.
然后我们看到了一个德怀特的访谈片段，我真的非常非常喜欢。

1680
01:16:28.370 --> 01:16:28.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1681
01:16:29.250 --> 01:16:31.930
He says, do I get along with my coworkers?
他说，我和同事相处得好吗？

1682
01:16:32.390 --> 01:16:34.510
Well, first of all, I don't have coworkers anymore.
嗯，首先，我不再有同事了。

1683
01:16:34.510 --> 01:16:35.750
I have subordinates.
我有的是下属。

1684
01:16:36.550 --> 01:16:39.850
And then he says he does get along with his subordinates.
然后他说他确实和他的下属相处得很好。

1685
01:16:40.010 --> 01:16:40.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1686
01:16:40.430 --> 01:16:43.210
And he kind of talks about each of us.
他谈到了我们每个人。

1687
01:16:43.370 --> 01:16:47.270
And there's little flashbacks to him spending time with us.
画面里穿插着他与我们相处的闪回片段。

1688
01:16:47.850 --> 01:16:48.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1689
01:16:48.250 --> 01:16:53.450
We learn that Meredith Palmer is the only person who knows how to properly headbang to Motorhead.
我们得知梅雷迪斯·帕尔默是唯一一个知道如何伴着摩托头乐队的音乐正确甩头的人。

1690
01:16:54.330 --> 01:16:57.070
Oscar is his godfather to his son.
奥斯卡是他儿子的教父。

1691
01:16:57.810 --> 01:17:00.650
Angela, his former accountant, is now his wife.
安吉拉，他以前的会计，现在是他的妻子。

1692
