01:23:49.490 --> 01:23:54.070
We're in the middle of some very sentimental sharing, but so is everybody else in the office.
我们正处在一段非常感性的分享中，办公室里的其他人也一样。

1862
01:23:54.230 --> 01:23:55.570
How about that for a transition?
这个转场怎么样？

1863
01:23:55.810 --> 01:23:56.410
I like it.
我很喜欢。

1864
01:23:56.410 --> 01:23:59.390
Oscar has one of my favorite final talking heads.
奥斯卡有我最喜欢的最终采访片段之一。

1865
01:23:59.590 --> 01:24:01.790
For me, it's really between Oscar and Ellie.
对我来说，我最喜欢奥斯卡和艾莉的。

1866
01:24:02.210 --> 01:24:07.030
I love that Oscar says, you take something ordinary like a piece of paper.
我喜欢奥斯卡说的那段话，你说拿一张普通的纸。

1867
01:24:07.190 --> 01:24:08.290
It's not much.
它没什么特别的。

1868
01:24:08.330 --> 01:24:15.590
But if you see it in the right way, and he's folding a piece of paper, he says, and that's what you did with this documentary.
但如果你以正确的视角去看它，他当时正在折纸，他说，你们拍这部纪录片也是这样。

1869
01:24:15.590 --> 01:24:18.350
And he holds up a little origami swan.
然后他举起了一只小折纸天鹅。

1870
01:24:19.350 --> 01:24:25.650
But then he says, but seriously, you made a nine-year documentary and you couldn't once show me doing my origami?
但接着他说，不过说真的，你们拍了九年的纪录片，竟然一次都没拍到我折纸？

1871
01:24:26.270 --> 01:24:28.270
He found a way to get it in there, though.
不过他还是想办法把它加进去了。

1872
01:24:28.270 --> 01:24:28.710
He did.
确实。

1873
01:24:29.050 --> 01:24:33.650
And now we're going to see Creed come out of the bathroom with no shirt on.
现在我们要看到克里德光着膀子从洗手间出来了。

1874
01:24:33.790 --> 01:24:34.670
He's brushing his teeth.
他在刷牙。

1875
01:24:34.970 --> 01:24:37.010
He clearly is living there again.
他显然又住在那儿了。

1876
01:24:37.550 --> 01:24:37.990
Yes.
没错。

1877
01:24:38.490 --> 01:24:44.350
It brings up a lot of questions like, I guess we don't use that closet or open that door.
这引出了很多问题，比如，我想我们平时不用那个壁橱，也不会打开那扇门。

1878
01:24:44.610 --> 01:24:45.130
Ever.
从来不用。

1879
01:24:45.930 --> 01:24:53.030
Everyone's very surprised to see him, but also very happy because he's going to get his guitar out and he's going to sing for us.
大家看到他都很惊讶，但也都很高兴，因为他要拿出吉他为我们唱歌了。

1880
01:24:53.290 --> 01:24:53.610
Yes.
是的。

1881
01:24:54.090 --> 01:24:59.010
We'll have more to say about Creed playing the guitar for all of us a little bit later.
关于克里德为我们弹吉他这件事，我们稍后再细说。

1882
01:24:59.870 --> 01:25:00.930
Yes, we will.
没错，我们会细说的。

1883
01:25:01.250 --> 01:25:03.230
Now Jim is going to have his talking head.
现在轮到吉姆的采访片段了。

1884
01:25:03.390 --> 01:25:06.110
He says, imagine going back and watching a tape of your life.
他说，想象一下回看自己人生的录像带。

1885
01:25:06.450 --> 01:25:10.070
You could see yourself change and make mistakes and grow up.
你可以看到自己的改变、犯错和成长。

1886
01:25:10.270 --> 01:25:14.790
You could watch yourself fall in love, watch yourself become a husband, become a father.
你可以看着自己坠入爱河，看着自己成为丈夫，成为父亲。

1887
01:25:14.790 --> 01:25:18.630
You guys gave that to me, and that's an amazing gift.
你们给了我这些，这是一份了不起的礼物。

1888
01:25:19.230 --> 01:25:22.450
I feel like there was a lot of John in this talking head.
我觉得这段采访里有很多约翰本人的影子。

1889
01:25:22.810 --> 01:25:24.250
Look what's on my document.
看我的文档上写了什么。

1890
01:25:24.590 --> 01:25:29.430
I put asterisk, I really saw John Krasinski in this talking head.
我加了星号，我真的在这段采访里看到了约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

1891
01:25:29.590 --> 01:25:29.810
Yeah.
没错。

1892
01:25:29.810 --> 01:25:30.790
That's John.
那就是约翰。

1893
01:25:31.150 --> 01:25:31.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1894
01:25:31.910 --> 01:25:35.550
All of those things happened to him in the course of this show.
所有这些事情都在这部剧的拍摄过程中发生在他身上了。

1895
01:25:35.810 --> 01:25:36.290
They did.
确实发生了。

1896
01:25:36.730 --> 01:25:37.690
It's true.
这是真的。

1897
01:25:38.130 --> 01:25:45.970
In this moment, we're kind of flashing back and forth between Creed playing his song and people having different conversations, different moments.
在这一刻，画面在克里德弹唱歌曲和人们进行各种对话、经历不同瞬间之间来回切换。

1898
01:25:45.970 --> 01:25:47.350
Different talking heads.
还有不同的采访片段。

1899
01:25:47.550 --> 01:25:47.970
Yes.
是的。

1900
01:25:48.390 --> 01:25:53.650
For example, Kevin is going to become so overcome with emotion, he tells Oscar he might be gay.
比如，凯文变得非常激动，他告诉奥斯卡他可能是同性恋。

1901
01:25:53.830 --> 01:25:55.150
And I love Oscar.
而且我爱奥斯卡。

1902
01:25:55.150 --> 01:25:55.850
You're not gay.
你又不是同性恋。

1903
01:25:56.270 --> 01:25:56.690
I know.
我知道。

1904
01:25:57.330 --> 01:25:59.630
Kevin is just feeling a lot of feelings.
凯文只是感触良多。

1905
01:26:00.270 --> 01:26:03.750
Erin is now going to have a talking head where she says, how did you do it?
艾琳现在要录一段采访，她会说，你们是怎么做到的？

1906
01:26:03.910 --> 01:26:06.290
How did you capture what it was really like?
你们是怎么捕捉到那种真实感的？

1907
01:26:06.410 --> 01:26:10.090
How we felt and how we made each other laugh and how we got through the day?
我们当时的感受，我们如何逗彼此发笑，以及我们如何度过每一天？

1908
01:26:10.390 --> 01:26:11.690
How did you do it?
你们是怎么做到的？

1909
01:26:12.210 --> 01:26:14.050
Also, how do cameras work?
还有，摄像机是怎么运作的？

1910
01:26:14.450 --> 01:26:16.110
I love her talking head.
我喜欢她的采访片段。

1911
01:26:16.230 --> 01:26:16.650
I know.
我知道。

1912
01:26:16.770 --> 01:26:17.470
It's really sweet.
真的很贴心。

1913
01:26:17.890 --> 01:26:22.050
Now, we have a fan question that I've placed here for a specific reason.
现在，有个粉丝提问，我把它放在这里是有特殊原因的。

1914
01:26:22.050 --> 01:26:23.570
It's from Lillian W.
来自加拿大安大略省的莉莲·W，她写道：为安吉拉讨回公道。

1915
01:26:23.850 --> 01:26:27.190
in Ontario, Canada, who wrote Justice for Angela.
我很难过安吉拉·马丁在结局里没有采访镜头。

1916
01:26:27.970 --> 01:26:32.470
I feel so badly that Angela Martin does not get a talking head in the finale.
有人能解释一下为什么吗？

1917
01:26:32.770 --> 01:26:34.070
Can someone explain why?
是不是拍了但没剪进最终版本里？

1918
01:26:34.330 --> 01:26:37.630
Was there one that was filmed and maybe didn't make the final cut?
安吉拉，你对此怎么看？

1919
01:26:37.850 --> 01:26:39.690
Angela, how do you feel about this?
嗯，其实拍了好几个。

1920
01:26:40.150 --> 01:26:41.310
Well, there were several.
你知道，DVD的删减片段里有很多没用上的素材。

1921
01:26:41.750 --> 01:26:47.190
You know, on the DVD, in the deleted scenes, there are so much footage that didn't make it.
不只是我的采访镜头。

1922
01:26:47.670 --> 01:26:49.610
And it wasn't just my talking head.
托比也有一个特别好笑的。

1923
01:26:49.770 --> 01:26:52.450
Toby also has one that's really funny.
但我确实有一个。

1924
01:26:52.850 --> 01:26:54.470
But I did have one.
而且，你知道，当剧集播出时发现我的采访镜头不在里面，我确实有点失落。

1925
01:26:54.790 --> 01:26:59.290
And, you know, when it aired and my talking head wasn't in it, I was a little bummed.
但那也是我的婚礼当天。

1926
01:26:59.390 --> 01:27:01.090
But it was also my wedding day.
我在这一集里有很多好玩的戏份。

1927
01:27:01.810 --> 01:27:03.810
I had a lot of fun stuff in this episode.
是啊。

1928
01:27:04.050 --> 01:27:04.230
Yeah.
如果你想听的话，现在可以放出来。

1929
01:27:04.710 --> 01:27:06.510
But here it is if you'd like to hear it.
我想听听。

1930
01:27:06.590 --> 01:27:07.430
I would like to hear it.
十年前，医生告诉我，我的脸部肌肉因为缺乏笑容而萎缩了。

1931
01:27:07.430 --> 01:27:12.570
Ten years ago, a doctor told me the muscles in my cheeks had atrophied from lack of smiling.
所以我得在睡前做锻炼。

1932
01:27:12.810 --> 01:27:15.250
So I had exercises to do at bedtime.
有点效果。

1933
01:27:15.450 --> 01:27:16.290
It helped some.
但现在我随时都在笑，甚至自己都没察觉。

1934
01:27:16.510 --> 01:27:20.110
But now I'm smiling all the time and I don't even notice.
所以，没错，我觉得我现在没那么刻薄了。

1935
01:27:20.970 --> 01:27:24.710
So, yeah, I think I'm less of a total bitch now.
那太搞笑了。

1936
01:27:27.250 --> 01:27:28.390
That's very funny.
我在整理数字杂物时发现了一张照片。

1937
01:27:29.150 --> 01:27:32.370
And I have a picture when I was looking through my digital clutter.
我录完采访后，格雷格·丹尼尔斯给我发了封邮件，他从侧面拍了一张我的照片。

1938
01:27:32.790 --> 01:27:38.530
Greg Daniels emailed me after I did my talking head and he took a picture of me from the side.
你可以看到摄像机。

1939
01:27:39.090 --> 01:27:40.530
You can see the camera.
你可以看到布莱恩·惠特尔在操作吊杆麦克风。

1940
01:27:40.790 --> 01:27:43.630
You can see Brian Whittle operating the boom.
我当时正对着摄像机，在会计部那边录采访。

1941
01:27:43.810 --> 01:27:47.090
And I'm facing camera giving the talking head over by accounting.
多棒的照片啊。

1942
01:27:47.330 --> 01:27:48.130
What a neat picture.
是啊。

1943
01:27:48.350 --> 01:27:48.490
Yeah.
达里尔会说，每天我来上班时，心里想的都是赶紧下班。

1944
01:27:49.350 --> 01:27:53.030
Daryl is going to say every day when I came into work, all I wanted to do was leave.
那为什么现在要离开时，感觉会这么难受呢？

1945
01:27:53.210 --> 01:27:56.230
So why in the world does it feel so hard to leave right now?
然后删减片段里还有一场戏。

1946
01:27:56.690 --> 01:27:59.510
And then there was a scene in the deleted scenes.
它甚至都不在拍摄剧本里。

1947
01:28:00.230 --> 01:28:02.130
It's not even in the shooting draft.
我觉得这是那种现场即兴发生的时刻之一。

1948
01:28:02.350 --> 01:28:05.250
I feel like this is one of those moments that happened on the day.
这就是我们上周提到的剧本重写的一部分，格雷格当时一直在增加或删减场景。

1949
01:28:05.250 --> 01:28:13.770
This was part of those rewrites of the script that we mentioned last week, how Greg was adding scenes, taking scenes away.
所以它们并不在所谓的拍摄剧本里。

1950
01:28:13.770 --> 01:28:18.110
So they were not in the sort of shooting draft.
而且我爱奥斯卡。

1951
01:28:18.390 --> 01:28:21.490
But you share what it is.
但你要分享它是什么。

1952
01:28:21.830 --> 01:28:26.370
This was originally Greg's idea for the ending shot.
这最初是格雷格对结尾镜头的构想。

1953
01:28:26.810 --> 01:28:26.990
Yeah.
没错。

1954
01:28:27.490 --> 01:28:31.330
So Daryl is going to ask everyone, who's been here the longest?
所以达里尔打算问大家，谁在这里待的时间最长？

1955
01:28:31.730 --> 01:28:33.970
And everyone starts to share their stories.
然后大家开始分享各自的故事。

1956
01:28:34.470 --> 01:28:36.550
The scene was so special to the caSt.
这一幕对演员们来说非常特别。

1957
01:28:36.890 --> 01:28:40.710
Everyone decides the person or thing that's been there the longest is that plant.
大家一致认为待在这里最久的人或物是那盆植物。

1958
01:28:41.270 --> 01:28:41.750
Planty.
小植。

1959
01:28:41.970 --> 01:28:42.450
Planty.
小植。

1960
01:28:42.610 --> 01:28:43.610
Let's hear this clip.
让我们听听这段片段。

1961
01:28:44.250 --> 01:28:45.490
Who's been here the longest?
谁在这里待的时间最长？

1962
01:28:45.950 --> 01:28:47.110
It was me.
是我。

1963
01:28:47.510 --> 01:28:48.390
Oh, it's me now.
噢，现在是我了。

1964
01:28:48.530 --> 01:28:49.950
I started two days after Stanley.
我比斯坦利晚两天入职。

1965
01:28:50.310 --> 01:28:52.370
Why do I remember working here before Stanley?
为什么我记得我比斯坦利更早在这里工作？

1966
01:28:52.630 --> 01:28:54.630
I'm pretty sure I was here before you, though.
不过我敢肯定我比你先到这里。

1967
01:28:54.890 --> 01:28:56.270
I'll tell you who's been here the longeSt.
我来告诉你们谁待的时间最长。

1968
01:28:56.690 --> 01:28:57.590
That poor plant.
那棵可怜的植物。

1969
01:28:59.030 --> 01:28:59.510
Planty.
小植。

1970
01:28:59.970 --> 01:29:00.450
Wait.
等等。

1971
01:29:00.830 --> 01:29:02.330
I don't remember that plant before.
我不记得以前有那盆植物。

1972
01:29:02.330 --> 01:29:04.270
That plant is a survivor.
那盆植物是个幸存者。

1973
01:29:05.230 --> 01:29:06.930
It's time for him to move on.
是时候让它离开了。

1974
01:29:08.330 --> 01:29:09.410
Let's set him free.
让我们放它自由吧。

1975
01:29:09.750 --> 01:29:10.550
Or her.
或者她。

1976
01:29:11.590 --> 01:29:12.070
Seriously.
说真的。

1977
01:29:12.290 --> 01:29:12.650
Come on.
来吧。

1978
01:29:12.890 --> 01:29:13.630
I'm just saying.
我只是随口说说。

1979
01:29:14.250 --> 01:29:17.450
Let's get him some real sunlight once and for all.
让我们一劳永逸地给它找点真正的阳光。

1980
01:29:17.710 --> 01:29:17.890
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1981
01:29:18.210 --> 01:29:18.370
Yes.
是的。

1982
01:29:18.770 --> 01:29:19.490
Somebody give me a hand.
谁来帮我一把。

1983
01:29:19.570 --> 01:29:20.010
I'm on it.
我来帮忙。

1984
01:29:20.330 --> 01:29:21.230
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1985
01:29:21.230 --> 01:29:22.490
We're really going to do this.
我们真的要这么做。

1986
01:29:23.410 --> 01:29:23.460
Okay.
好的。

1987
01:29:23.460 --> 01:29:23.830
All right.
行吧。

1988
01:29:24.190 --> 01:29:24.590
Yeah.
没错。

1989
01:29:39.580 --> 01:29:41.680
Don't overpack the dirt.
别把土压得太实。

1990
01:29:41.880 --> 01:29:42.860
Ah, amateurs.
啊，外行。

1991
01:29:43.900 --> 01:29:45.120
Office plant.
办公室植物。

1992
01:29:45.300 --> 01:29:46.760
Office plant.
办公室植物。

1993
01:29:46.960 --> 01:29:48.320
Office plant.
办公室植物。

1994
01:29:48.580 --> 01:29:49.920
Office plant.
办公室植物。

1995
01:29:50.160 --> 01:29:51.400
Office plant.
办公室植物。

1996
01:29:51.640 --> 01:29:52.020
Yeah.
没错。

1997
01:29:56.480 --> 01:29:58.200
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍摄那场戏的情景。

1998
01:29:58.340 --> 01:30:01.440
And I have so many pictures from all of us outside.
而且我有很多我们大家在户外的照片。

1999
01:30:01.920 --> 01:30:02.420
Yes.
是的。

2000
01:30:02.420 --> 01:30:04.420
It was a really special moment for the caSt.
这对演员们来说确实是一个非常特别的时刻。

2001
01:30:04.580 --> 01:30:06.320
We all stand around planty.
我们都站在Planty周围。

2002
01:30:06.580 --> 01:30:09.720
And it's just one of the moments I remember so vividly.
那是我记忆中非常深刻的瞬间之一。

2003
01:30:09.720 --> 01:30:21.120
So, originally, the idea was that the episode was going to end, like, the final shot of the episode was going to be of planty.
最初的想法是，这一集要结束时，最后一个镜头应该是Planty。

2004
01:30:21.200 --> 01:30:28.060
And the idea was just, like, that this thing was going to, like, continue to grow.
当时的想法就是，这东西会一直生长下去。

2005
01:30:28.300 --> 01:30:28.800
Yes.
是的。

2006
01:30:28.960 --> 01:30:31.640
You know, after a lot of us have moved on.
你知道，在我们很多人离开之后。

2007
01:30:31.780 --> 01:30:37.060
I went to the very final line of the script for the shooting draft, and this is what it says.
我翻看了拍摄剧本的最后一行，上面是这样写的。

2008
01:30:37.060 --> 01:30:43.540
B-roll of the replanted office plant with Dunder Mifflin behind it as the sun comes up over the parking lot.
空镜：重新种好的办公室盆栽，背景是邓德·米夫林公司，太阳在停车场上方升起。

2009
01:30:43.700 --> 01:30:44.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

2010
01:30:44.440 --> 01:30:46.900
But we're going to end a slightly different way.
但我们打算用稍微不同的方式结束。

2011
01:30:47.080 --> 01:30:47.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

2012
01:30:47.640 --> 01:30:49.900
We're going to have some more talking heads.
我们会有更多的采访镜头。

2013
01:30:49.900 --> 01:30:53.040
We're going to see Creed get arrested.
我们会看到克里德被捕。

2014
01:30:53.600 --> 01:30:54.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

2015
01:30:54.460 --> 01:30:56.440
Meredith and Phyllis are going to share.
梅雷迪思和菲利斯会分享一些事。

2016
01:30:57.280 --> 01:31:05.000
And this is all kind of intercut with scenes of us gathering up our things and leaving for the final time.
所有这些镜头会穿插在我们收拾东西最后一次离开的场景中。

2017
01:31:05.000 --> 01:31:05.740
Yes.
是的。

2018
01:31:05.940 --> 01:31:13.980
If you go to 48 minutes and 14 seconds, that shot of all of us leaving was actually the last shot we filmed together as a caSt.
如果你看到48分14秒，那个我们所有人离开的镜头，实际上是我们作为演员阵容最后一起拍摄的镜头。

2019
01:31:14.260 --> 01:31:14.720
Yeah.
是的。

2020
01:31:14.980 --> 01:31:17.520
So, Pam has the final talking head.
所以，帕姆有最后的采访镜头。

2021
01:31:17.660 --> 01:31:25.080
And when the one-liner, which is the schedule of scenes for an episode, comes out, you know I would love to read it.
当通告单——也就是一集拍摄场景的时间表——出来时，你知道我总是很想看。

2022
01:31:25.200 --> 01:31:25.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

2023
01:31:25.580 --> 01:31:33.300
I saw that the very last thing that was scheduled for the last day of shooting was Pam's talking head.
我看到拍摄最后一天安排的最后一件事是帕姆的采访。

2024
01:31:33.760 --> 01:31:38.140
I went to John's trailer, and I said, John, did you see the one-liner?
我去了约翰的拖车，我说，约翰，你看到通告单了吗？

2025
01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:42.480
And I showed him, and I said, I don't want to be here alone.
我给他看了，我说，我不想一个人待在那儿。

2026
01:31:43.000 --> 01:31:45.180
I don't want to be here all by myself.
我不想独自一人待在那儿。

2027
01:31:45.820 --> 01:31:46.280
Yeah.
是的。

2028
01:31:46.280 --> 01:31:48.100
I want us to end together.
我想我们一起结束。

2029
01:31:48.380 --> 01:31:50.440
And John said, we have to end together.
约翰说，我们必须一起结束。

2030
01:31:51.080 --> 01:32:06.520
So we went together to Ken Kwapis and Greg, and they said, oh, we thought it would be really poetic to end the show by filming the very last moment last, but we hear you.
所以我们一起去找了肯·夸皮斯和格雷格，他们说，哦，我们觉得如果把最后一刻留在最后拍会很有诗意，但我们听你们的。

2031
01:32:06.520 --> 01:32:08.260
So here's what we'll do.
所以我们这样安排。

2032
01:32:08.640 --> 01:32:12.360
We're going to film your talking head, if everyone doesn't mind waiting.
如果大家不介意等待的话，我们就先拍你的采访。

2033
01:32:13.020 --> 01:32:21.620
And then when you're finished, we will film that final B-roll of everyone leaving the office and of Pam taking the watercolor off the wall.
等你拍完，我们再拍那个大家离开办公室以及帕姆把水彩画从墙上取下来的最终空镜。

2034
01:32:21.780 --> 01:32:22.720
How does that sound?
你们觉得怎么样？

2035
01:32:23.000 --> 01:32:29.980
And John and I were like, yes, we need to all be together when you say that's a wrap on The Office.
约翰和我当时就说，太好了，当你们宣布《办公室》杀青时，我们需要所有人都在场。

2036
01:32:30.500 --> 01:32:32.180
That's a series wrap.
那是全剧杀青。

2037
01:32:32.360 --> 01:32:33.940
I'm like, I don't want to be here by myself.
我当时想，我可不想独自待在那儿。

2038
01:32:34.100 --> 01:32:34.280
Yeah.
是的。

2039
01:32:34.620 --> 01:32:34.780
Yeah.
是的。

2040
01:32:35.440 --> 01:32:36.860
And that's what they did.
他们就是这么做的。

2041
01:32:36.860 --> 01:32:38.780
And we were all so thankful.
我们都非常感激。

2042
01:32:39.460 --> 01:32:43.700
And, you know, I have video of all of us watching you do that talking head.
你知道，我拍了视频，记录了我们所有人看着你做那个采访的过程。

2043
01:32:43.960 --> 01:32:45.860
I'm finally going to post it.
我终于要把它发出来了。

2044
01:32:46.020 --> 01:32:47.740
I've been saving it for years.
我保存了好多年了。

2045
01:32:49.120 --> 01:32:57.120
And it was just really moving that when they said that's a wrap, that we all just poured into the bullpen.
当他们宣布杀青时，我们所有人都涌向办公区，那一幕真的非常感人。

2046
01:32:57.360 --> 01:33:03.040
Our crew, our writers were all standing around waiting, watching with us on the stage.
我们的剧组人员、编剧们都站在周围等着，和我们一起在片场看着。

2047
01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:06.380
And we all just hugged and cried, all of us.
我们所有人都拥抱在一起，哭成一团。

2048
01:33:06.800 --> 01:33:10.240
Well, we did that exit way more times than we needed to.
其实我们拍那个离开的镜头比需要的次数多多了。

2049
01:33:10.480 --> 01:33:10.980
I know.
我知道。

2050
01:33:10.980 --> 01:33:18.240
And Ken Kwapis said, after about like six times, he turned to Greg and he said, Greg, I think we got it.
肯·夸皮斯在大约拍了六次之后，转头对格雷格说，格雷格，我想我们拍到了。

2051
01:33:18.520 --> 01:33:18.940
We're done.
我们拍完了。

2052
01:33:19.220 --> 01:33:21.180
And Greg said, what do we do?
格雷格问，我们该怎么办？

2053
01:33:21.840 --> 01:33:28.420
And Ken said, well, we have to say that's a wrap, but I think you should say it, Greg.
肯说，好吧，我们得宣布杀青了，但我认为应该由你来说，格雷格。

2054
01:33:29.380 --> 01:33:32.140
So he said, I'll have him do it one more time, okay?
于是他说，我会让他再来一次，好吗？

2055
01:33:32.440 --> 01:33:33.700
And Greg was like, okay.
格雷格说，好的。

2056
01:33:34.120 --> 01:33:35.860
So we did it one more time.
所以我们又拍了一次。

2057
01:33:36.160 --> 01:33:40.400
And I remember every time we would leave, we would crowd.
我记得每次我们要离开时，我们都会挤在一起。

2058
01:33:40.480 --> 01:33:43.940
All of us would crowd into that little area by the elevator.
我们所有人都会挤在电梯旁那块小区域里。

2059
01:33:44.400 --> 01:33:46.680
And we would stand there for a beat.
我们会站在那里等一会儿。

2060
01:33:47.040 --> 01:33:52.060
And then you would hear them say, all right, reset, back to one, going again.
然后你会听到他们说，好了，重置，回到起点，再来一次。

2061
01:33:53.560 --> 01:33:56.420
And there was always this very pregnant pause.
当时总会有一段意味深长的停顿。

2062
01:33:56.560 --> 01:34:01.760
Like once we got to like take three, take four, you're like, how many times can we do this?
拍到第三条、第四条的时候，你就会想，我们到底要拍多少次？

2063
01:34:02.240 --> 01:34:06.100
And then finally, we were all standing there in that like pregnant pause.
最后，我们都站在那段意味深长的停顿中。

2064
01:34:06.240 --> 01:34:07.720
And we heard Greg's voice.
我们听到了格雷格的声音。

2065
01:34:07.900 --> 01:34:08.020
Yeah.
是的。

2066
01:34:08.020 --> 01:34:13.520
He said, cut, that's a wrap, that's a series wrap on the office.
他说，卡，杀青了，这是《办公室》全剧的杀青。

2067
01:34:13.780 --> 01:34:18.000
And then we all came out from that area.
然后我们都从那个区域走了出来。

2068
01:34:18.300 --> 01:34:21.780
And we were surprised by our crew that they had had gather.
我们被聚集在那里的剧组成员给惊喜到了。

2069
01:34:22.680 --> 01:34:22.840
Yeah.
是的。

2070
01:34:23.620 --> 01:34:27.180
Every time we walked to the elevator bank, I was next to Phyllis.
每次我们走向电梯间时，我都在菲利斯旁边。

2071
01:34:27.300 --> 01:34:32.340
Because when you watch the scene, Dwight goes to help with the plant.
因为当你观看那个场景时，德怀特去帮忙搬植物了。

2072
01:34:32.340 --> 01:34:35.220
And I'm kind of left perched on top of front reception.
而我当时正坐在前台接待处上面。

2073
01:34:35.220 --> 01:34:36.140
It's pretty high.
那里挺高的。

2074
01:34:37.100 --> 01:34:39.700
And Phyllis and Oscar would help me down.
菲利斯和奥斯卡会扶我下来。

2075
01:34:40.340 --> 01:34:42.100
So I would walk out with them.
所以我总是和他们一起走出来。

2076
01:34:42.260 --> 01:34:46.180
And Phyllis and I would hold hands waiting to see if we would go again.
菲利斯和我手牵着手，等着看是否还要再拍一次。

2077
01:34:47.860 --> 01:34:48.460
Yeah.
是的。

2078
01:34:49.180 --> 01:34:52.140
That was pretty emotional.
那真的很感人。

2079
01:34:53.740 --> 01:34:58.220
But the episode ends after Pam's talking head.
但这一集是在帕姆的采访镜头后结束的。

2080
01:34:59.140 --> 01:34:59.740
Yes.
没错。

2081
01:34:59.900 --> 01:35:03.260
Pam famously says there's a lot of beauty in ordinary things.
帕姆那句名言说，平凡的事物中蕴含着许多美。

2082
01:35:03.380 --> 01:35:04.560
Isn't that kind of the point?
这不正是这部剧的意义所在吗？

2083
01:35:04.560 --> 01:35:10.300
Well, that's just, that was Greg's philosophy of this show.
嗯，那正是格雷格对这部剧的理念。

2084
01:35:10.540 --> 01:35:17.520
It was meant to mine the beauty in ordinary day-to-day life.
它的初衷就是挖掘平凡日常生活中蕴含的美。

2085
01:35:17.820 --> 01:35:18.780
It's beautiful.
太美了。

2086
01:35:19.120 --> 01:35:19.280
Yeah.
是的。

2087
01:35:19.440 --> 01:35:21.420
That's what we were shining a spotlight on.
这就是我们想要聚焦的地方。

2088
01:35:22.280 --> 01:35:23.640
So amazing.
太棒了。

2089
01:35:27.260 --> 01:35:29.660
And I loved shooting this talking head.
我非常喜欢拍摄这个采访镜头。

2090
01:35:29.840 --> 01:35:31.340
I was talking to Ken Quapis.
当时我在和肯·夸皮斯交谈。

2091
01:35:31.480 --> 01:35:35.800
That's who was sitting across from me in the job when Jim finally asked Pam on a date.
吉姆最终约帕姆出去约会时，就是他坐在我对面。

2092
01:35:36.260 --> 01:35:39.480
And that's who I got to deliver my final talking head to.
而我正是对着他完成了我最后一个采访镜头。

2093
01:35:40.240 --> 01:35:42.180
And it's very meaningful to me.
这对我来说意义非凡。

2094
01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:47.280
I love that we see Steve again one last time.
我很高兴我们最后又见到了史蒂夫。

2095
01:35:47.560 --> 01:35:49.760
I love that we get to see Michael.
我很高兴我们能看到迈克尔。

2096
01:35:50.020 --> 01:35:51.960
And he's hanging Hope in a frame.
他正在把“希望”挂进相框里。

2097
01:35:52.320 --> 01:35:52.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

2098
01:35:53.100 --> 01:35:54.000
That's right.
没错。

2099
01:35:54.460 --> 01:36:01.100
And then that sort of morphs into our actual building.
然后画面过渡到了我们真实的办公楼。

2100
01:36:01.100 --> 01:36:04.620
They sort of go from the watercolor to the actual Dunder Mifflin.
他们从水彩画过渡到了真实的邓德·米夫林公司。

2101
01:36:04.780 --> 01:36:05.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2102
01:36:05.220 --> 01:36:07.520
And I love how plain it is.
而且我喜欢它那种朴实无华的感觉。

2103
01:36:07.960 --> 01:36:13.840
I love, it's literally the most ordinary-looking building you could imagine.
我喜欢，它真的是你能想象到的最普通的一栋建筑了。

2104
01:36:13.980 --> 01:36:14.160
Yeah.
没错。

2105
01:36:14.320 --> 01:36:15.540
And that was our building.
那正是我们的办公楼。

2106
01:36:15.860 --> 01:36:16.140
Yeah.
是啊。

2107
01:36:16.580 --> 01:36:19.140
And Pam gets to take her painting home.
帕姆可以把她的画带回家了。

2108
01:36:19.320 --> 01:36:20.920
And Jenna took it home, too.
珍娜也把它带回家了。

2109
01:36:21.440 --> 01:36:22.900
It's in my living room.
它现在就在我的客厅里。

2110
01:36:24.020 --> 01:36:31.860
Well, guys, that is finale part two, but we're not finished yet because from the moment we
好了，各位，这就是大结局的下半部分，但我们还没结束，因为从我们开始做这个播客的那一刻起，

2111
01:36:31.860 --> 01:36:36.200
started this podcast, we knew exactly how we wanted to end it.
我们就确切地知道该如何收尾。

2112
01:36:36.400 --> 01:36:37.260
We did.
确实。

2113
01:36:37.580 --> 01:36:45.020
And my neighbor is coming through for us because we reached out to Creed Bratton and we said,
而且我的邻居帮了我们大忙，因为我们联系了克里德·布拉顿，我们说，

2114
01:36:45.160 --> 01:36:48.400
Creed, will you sing your song on our podcast, All the Faces?
克里德，你愿意在我们的播客上唱你的那首歌《所有的面孔》吗？

2115
01:36:48.780 --> 01:36:52.320
That's the perfect way to say goodbye to this rewatch.
那是告别这次重温之旅的完美方式。

2116
01:36:52.320 --> 01:36:54.920
And he said yes, and he's here today.
他说愿意，而且他今天就在这儿。

2117
01:36:55.620 --> 01:37:01.100
So give us a second, which to you will literally feel like one second, and he's going to set
所以给我们一秒钟时间，对你们来说这真的就像一秒钟一样，他会准备好，

2118
01:37:01.100 --> 01:37:03.240
up and we'll chat with him.
然后我们会和他聊天。

2119
01:37:07.480 --> 01:37:10.600
Well, here is our special guest we've been talking about.
好了，这就是我们一直提到的特别嘉宾。

2120
01:37:10.600 --> 01:37:11.660
We are so excited.
我们太兴奋了。

2121
01:37:11.840 --> 01:37:18.060
In fact, our very first guest in our new space here to celebrate the end of the rewatch with
事实上，我们新空间里的第一位嘉宾，来和我们一起庆祝重温之旅结束的，

2122
01:37:18.060 --> 01:37:19.620
us is Creed Bratton.
就是克里德·布拉顿。

2123
01:37:19.820 --> 01:37:20.480
Hi, Creed.
你好，克里德。

2124
01:37:20.780 --> 01:37:21.380
Hi, ladies.
你们好，女士们。

2125
01:37:21.740 --> 01:37:22.800
Thanks for having me.
谢谢你们邀请我。

2126
01:37:23.140 --> 01:37:23.880
Yes, thank you.
不客气，谢谢你。

2127
01:37:24.220 --> 01:37:25.160
You are here.
你真的来了。

2128
01:37:25.160 --> 01:37:28.280
You are going to be leaving tomorrow.
你明天就要离开了。

2129
01:37:28.320 --> 01:37:31.620
We got you on your last day in town.
我们正好赶在你留在城里的最后一天见到了你。

2130
01:37:31.920 --> 01:37:33.040
Tell everybody where you're going.
告诉大家你要去哪儿。

2131
01:37:33.320 --> 01:37:42.190
I'll be in Ireland and England, Norway, Denmark, Holland, Slovakia, and Czechoslovakia.
我要去爱尔兰、英国、挪威、丹麦、荷兰、斯洛伐克和捷克斯洛伐克。

2132
01:37:42.940 --> 01:37:43.680
On tour.
去巡演。

2133
01:37:43.960 --> 01:37:45.240
On tour for the month of October.
十月份整整一个月都在巡演。

2134
01:37:45.580 --> 01:37:46.080
Amazing.
太棒了。

2135
01:37:46.320 --> 01:37:48.820
We're going to put all of your tour dates in our Instagram.
我们会把你的所有巡演日期发到我们的Instagram上。

2136
01:37:48.820 --> 01:37:49.500
Oh, thank you.
哦，谢谢。

2137
01:37:49.600 --> 01:37:49.840
Yes.
是的。

2138
01:37:50.000 --> 01:37:50.400
Thank you.
谢谢。

2139
01:37:50.580 --> 01:37:53.440
And then we're so thrilled because you are here today.
而且我们非常激动，因为你今天能来。

2140
01:37:53.740 --> 01:37:57.480
This was actually something Jenna and I have talked about for years, and then you brought
这其实是珍娜和我谈论了多年的事情，然后你又把它提了出来，克里德。

2141
01:37:57.480 --> 01:37:59.080
it back up to us, Creed.
但我那次是意外打来的。

2142
01:37:59.160 --> 01:38:00.440
But I called it accidentally that time.
你能告诉大家你真的是意外打来的吗？

2143
01:38:01.080 --> 01:38:04.600
And will you tell everybody you really have called accidentally?
你知道，网上的人以为那是我们安排好的。

2144
01:38:04.860 --> 01:38:07.280
You know, online, people think that we set that up.
不，不，伙计们。

2145
01:38:07.280 --> 01:38:08.100
No, no folks.
不，你真的是刚好打过来了。

2146
01:38:08.100 --> 01:38:09.200
No, you really just called.
《办公室》的粉丝们，女士们。

2147
01:38:09.220 --> 01:38:09.760
Fans of the office, ladies.
我只是打来问候一下，因为我很好奇你们看到剧集的哪里了。

2148
01:38:10.040 --> 01:38:14.820
I just called to check in because I was curious to see where you guys were on the show.
我想，你知道，我打给“南瓜”问候一下吧。

2149
01:38:14.920 --> 01:38:17.100
And I thought, you know, I'll call Pumpkin and check in.
然后你就真的打了。

2150
01:38:17.380 --> 01:38:18.180
And you did.
你确实打了。

2151
01:38:18.280 --> 01:38:18.860
And I did.
我确实这么做了。

2152
01:38:18.960 --> 01:38:20.120
And then you guys were on the air.
然后你们就上节目了。

2153
01:38:20.320 --> 01:38:21.680
So no, that's honest to God.
所以不，那是千真万确的。

2154
01:38:21.840 --> 01:38:25.000
And I know Creed lies, but myself as Creed, I don't lie.
我知道克里德会撒谎，但作为克里德本人，我从不撒谎。

2155
01:38:25.120 --> 01:38:25.760
That's true.
那是真的。

2156
01:38:25.940 --> 01:38:26.700
That the character does.
那个角色确实会撒谎。

2157
01:38:26.900 --> 01:38:30.900
Well, this song is one that you sang on the finale.
嗯，这首歌是你在大结局里唱的那首。

2158
01:38:31.320 --> 01:38:31.980
That's right.
没错。

2159
01:38:37.280 --> 01:38:41.540
I'm in, it's probably about, I don't know, how long was it before we did the table read?
我当时在场，大概是……我不知道，距离我们围读剧本还有多久？

2160
01:38:41.600 --> 01:38:45.880
You know, before we did the table read, a month and a half, a month, a month, at least
你知道，在围读剧本之前，大概一个半月，一个月，一个月，至少一个月吧。

2161
01:38:45.880 --> 01:38:46.560
over a month.
超过一个月。

2162
01:38:47.320 --> 01:38:53.320
So I'm in my trailer, and we've all been talking, how are we going to possibly end this
当时我在拖车里，我们都在讨论，我们该怎么给这部剧画上句号，

2163
01:38:53.320 --> 01:38:55.460
show, this amazing show that we all love?
这部我们大家都深爱的精彩剧集？

2164
01:38:55.680 --> 01:38:57.140
What are we going to do for the finale?
大结局我们要拍什么？

2165
01:38:57.280 --> 01:38:58.340
It's got to be amazing.
一定要非常精彩才行。

2166
01:38:58.760 --> 01:39:03.420
Now, Greg Daniels came back to right the ship and do it with us, you know?
格雷格·丹尼尔斯回来拨乱反正，和我们一起完成它，你懂的。

2167
01:39:03.880 --> 01:39:06.860
So I'm sitting in my trailer, and there's a knock on the door, and it's a PA.
所以我坐在拖车里，有人敲门，是个制片助理。

